#. ~ Description of "Magic 8-Ball"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid ""
"A fortune-telling device from the 1950s.  The kind of moral support you "
"didn't know you needed."
msgstr "1950年代に流行った占い装置です。特に必要のない精神的助言を与えてくれます。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "deck of cards"
msgid_plural "decks of cards"
msgstr[0] "ゲームセット(トランプ)"

#. ~ Description of "deck of cards"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "A deck of 52 playing cards."
msgstr "52枚揃ったトランプカードです。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "makeshift deck of cards"
msgid_plural "makeshift decks of cards"
msgstr[0] "トランプ"

#. ~ Description of "makeshift deck of cards"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid ""
"A deck of 52 makeshift cards, made out of cardboard rectangles with simple "
"designs drawn on them."
msgstr "長方形の厚紙にシンプルなデザインが描かれた、手製の52枚のトランプカードです。"

#. ~ Unique mission item for the CITY_COP.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "family photo"
msgid_plural "family photos"
msgstr[0] "家族の写真"

#. ~ Unique mission item for the CITY_COP.
#. ~ Description of "family photo"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid ""
"A photo of a smiling family on a camping trip.  One of the parents looks "
"like a cleaner, happier version of the person you know."
msgstr "キャンプ旅行中に撮影された、にこやかに笑う家族の写真です。両親の内の一人は、今の姿よりずっと清潔で幸せそうに見えます。"

#. ~ The pom poms could make use of their own type of use_action.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "pair of pom poms"
msgid_plural "pairs of pom poms"
msgstr[0] "ポンポン"

#. ~ The pom poms could make use of their own type of use_action.
#. ~ Description of "pair of pom poms"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid ""
"A pair of red and silver pom poms with plastic handles.  Using them will "
"make you start a cheerleading routine."
msgstr "プラスチック製の持ち手が付いた、赤色と銀色のポンポンです。使用するとチアダンスを踊ります。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "polaroid photo"
msgid_plural "polaroid photos"
msgstr[0] "ポラロイド写真"

#. ~ Description of "polaroid photo"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid ""
"A poorly taken polaroid photo of a young man wearing bell-bottoms and a "
"fedora.  It's pretty blurry."
msgstr "ベルボトムと中折れ帽を身に着けている若者が不鮮明に映ったポラロイド写真です。写真はかなりぼやけています。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "chess set"
msgid_plural "chess sets"
msgstr[0] "ゲームセット(チェス)"

#. ~ Description of "chess set"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid ""
"A wooden box containing all the equipment needed to play a game of chess."
msgstr "チェスゲームに必要な全ての道具が入った木箱です。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "checkers set"
msgid_plural "checkers sets"
msgstr[0] "ゲームセット(チェッカー)"

#. ~ Description of "checkers set"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "A wooden box containing a set of round tokens used to play checkers."
msgstr "チェッカーに使う丸い駒が入った木箱です。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "deck of Sorcery cards"
msgid_plural "decks of Sorcery cards"
msgstr[0] "ゲームセット(ソーサリー)"

#. ~ Description of "deck of Sorcery cards"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid ""
"A set of cards meant to play the game \"Sorcery.\"  Each card has a fun "
"picture of a different monster."
msgstr "「ソーサリー」というゲームで遊ぶためのカード一式です。各カードには多種多様なモンスターの絵が描かれています。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "Picturesque"
msgid_plural "sets of Picturesque"
msgstr[0] "ゲームセット(ピクチャレスク)"

#. ~ Description of "Picturesque"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid ""
"A game where one draws an image, and the others attempt to guess what it is."
msgstr "一人が絵を描いて、それを見たもう一人が何を描いたのか当てるゲームです。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "Capitalism"
msgid_plural "sets of Capitalism"
msgstr[0] "ゲームセット(キャピタリズム)"

#. ~ Description of "Capitalism"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid ""
"A game where players traverse around the board buying property and swindling"
" their friends."
msgstr "盤上の駒を動かして資産を買ったり友人を騙したりして遊ぶゲームです。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "Blobs and Bandits"
msgid_plural "sets of Blobs and Bandits"
msgstr[0] "ゲームセット(ブロブス&バンディッツ)"

#. ~ Description of "Blobs and Bandits"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid ""
"A roleplaying game set in the post-apocalypse, so you can pretend to survive"
" the apocalypse while surviving the apocalypse."
msgstr ""
"ポストアポカリプスの世界を舞台にしたテーブルトークRPGです。現実の終末世界をサバイバルしながら、ゲーム内でも終末世界のサバイバルごっこを楽しめます。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "Battlehammer"
msgid_plural "sets of Battlehammer"
msgstr[0] "ゲームセット(バトルハンマー)"

#. ~ Description of "Battlehammer"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid ""
"A strategy game featuring a set of tiny figurines of fantasy creatures."
msgstr "ファンタジー世界の生き物を模した小さなフィギュアを使って遊ぶストラテジーゲームです。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "Battlehammer 20k"
msgid_plural "sets of Battlehammer 20k"
msgstr[0] "ゲームセット(バトルハンマー20k)"

#. ~ Description of "Battlehammer 20k"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid ""
"A strategy game featuring a set of tiny figurines of space aliens and "
"grotesque space marines."
msgstr "宇宙人やグロテスクなスペースマリーンを模した小さなフィギュアを使って遊ぶストラテジーゲームです。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "Settlers of the Ranch"
msgid_plural "sets of Settlers of the Ranch"
msgstr[0] "ゲームセット(大農園の開拓者たち)"

#. ~ Description of "Settlers of the Ranch"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid ""
"A strategy game where players build settlements and trade for supplies."
msgstr "プレイヤー同士が開拓地で資源を売買するストラテジーゲームです。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "senet set"
msgid_plural "senet sets"
msgstr[0] "ゲームセット(セネト)"

#. ~ Description of "senet set"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid ""
"A wooden box containing all the pieces needed to play a game of senet, and "
"also a extremely small guide of how to play it.  Board game from ancient "
"Egypt, it plays as modern chess with 3x10 grid and small amount of pieces."
msgstr ""
"小箱の中に、セネトをプレイするために必要な全ての駒と、遊び方が書かれた小さな紙が入っています。セネトは古代エジプトのボードゲームであり、3x10のマス目といくつかの駒を使って、現代のチェスに似たルールで遊びます。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "mahjong set"
msgid_plural "mahjong sets"
msgstr[0] "ゲームセット(麻雀)"

#. ~ Description of "mahjong set"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid ""
"A very beautiful, and really huge plastic box, that contain all the pieces "
"needed to play a game of mahjong, and also a extremely small, apparently "
"poorly translated but comprehensible guide of how to play it.  Mahjong is a "
"tile-based game where you need to find pairs of pieces and take the biggest "
"score."
msgstr ""
"非常に美しいデザインの大型プラスチックケースの中に、麻雀をプレイするために必要な全ての牌と、翻訳が不十分ながら分かりやすい言葉で遊び方が書かれた紙が入っています。麻雀は牌同士を組み合わせて役を作り、一番点数が高い者が勝つゲームです。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "chaturanga chess set"
msgid_plural "chaturanga chess sets"
msgstr[0] "ゲームセット(チャトランガ)"

#. ~ Description of "chaturanga chess set"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid ""
"A polished wooden box containing all the pieces needed to play a game of "
"chaturanga chess, and also a extremely small guide of how to play it.  "
"Chaturanga is an ancient Indian strategy game, the ancestor of the many "
"another chess variations - the European, Chinese, Japanese chess etc)."
msgstr ""
"艶のある木箱の中に、チャトランガのプレイに必要な全ての駒と、遊び方が書かれた紙が入っています。チャトランガは古代インドの戦略ゲームで、ヨーロッパのチェス、中国や日本の将棋の祖先にあたります。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "backgammon set"
msgid_plural "backgammon sets"
msgstr[0] "ゲームセット(バックギャモン)"

#. ~ Description of "backgammon set"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid ""
"A very nice dark wooden box containing all the pieces needed to play a game "
"of backgammon, and also a extremely small handwritten guide of how to play "
"it.  Backgammon is a two-player board game played with counters and dice on "
"table boards.  The objective of the game is to move the fifteen pieces "
"around the board and be first to remove them from the board"
msgstr ""
"デザインが非常にお洒落なダークウッドの箱の中に、バックギャモンのプレイに必要な全ての駒と、遊び方が手書きされた紙が入っています。バックギャモンは2人用のボードゲームで、盤上に駒とサイコロを置いて遊びます。15個の駒を盤上で動かし、全ての駒を一番先にゴールさせた者が勝利します。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "latrunculi set"
msgid_plural "latrunculi sets"
msgstr[0] "ゲームセット(ラトゥンクリ)"

#. ~ Description of "latrunculi set"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid ""
"A small wooden box containing all the pieces needed to play a game of "
"latrunculi, and also a extremely small guide of how to play it. Two-player "
"strategy board game which was played throughout the Roman Empire in the "
"past, its require a lot of tactic and strategy."
msgstr ""
"小さな木箱の中に、ラトゥンクリのプレイに必要な全ての駒と、遊び方が書かれた小さな紙が入っています。ラトゥンクリは戦術と戦略を駆使して遊ぶ2人用のボードゲームで、かつてはローマ帝国全域で親しまれていました。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "go set"
msgid_plural "go sets"
msgstr[0] "ゲームセット(囲碁)"

#. ~ Description of "go set"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid ""
"A wooden box containing all the pieces needed to play a game of go, and also"
" a extremely small guide of how to play it, where one side seems to be "
"written in the Mandarin language and the other side seems to be in English."
"  It is two-player game, where each tries to grab more territory than the "
"enemy."
msgstr ""
"木箱の中に、囲碁のプレイに必要な全ての石と、中国語と思しき文字と英語で遊び方が書かれた小さな紙が入っています。囲碁は2人用のゲームで、相手より多くの陣地を囲った者が勝ちます。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "shogi set"
msgid_plural "shogi sets"
msgstr[0] "ゲームセット(将棋)"

#. ~ Description of "shogi set"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid ""
"A wooden box containing all the pieces needed to play a game of shogi, and "
"also a extremely small guide of how to play it, with some letters in "
"Japanese.  Also known as Japanese chess, it is a strategy board game for two"
" players.  It was once one of the most popular board games in Japan, before "
"the Cataclysm, and the main objective is to, though strategy, tsumi "
"(checkmate) the opponent's osho (king)."
msgstr ""
"木箱の中に、将棋のプレイに必要な全ての駒と、日本語と思しき文字で遊び方が書かれた小さな紙が入っています。将棋は日本のチェスとも言われる、2人用の戦略ゲームです。戦国時代以前から存在する日本で人気の高いボードゲームの一つであり、相手の王将(キング)を戦略的に詰み(チェックメイト)状態にすれば勝利です。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "hnefatafl set"
msgid_plural "hnefatafl sets"
msgstr[0] "ゲームセット(ネファタフル)"

#. ~ Description of "hnefatafl set"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid ""
"A wooden box containing all the pieces needed to play a game of hnefatafl, "
"and also a extremely small guide of how to play it, with some nordic rules "
"written on it.  Also called 'Viking Chess', it was a popular game in "
"medieval Scandinavia, there are the attackers and defenders, the attackers "
"(located in the sides of the board), must capture the defenders king, while "
"the defenders should get the king to one of the four corners of the board."
msgstr ""
"木箱の中に、ネファタフルのプレイに必要な全ての駒と、当時の北欧でのルールが書かれた小さな紙が入っています。ネファフタルは「バイキングチェス」とも言われる、中世時代にスカンジナビア地方で流行したゲームです。攻撃者と防御者に分かれ、攻撃者は(盤の側面に置かれた)防御者のキングを捕らえれば勝利し、防御者はキングを盤の四隅のいずれかに移動させれば勝利します。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "alquerque set"
msgid_plural "alquerque sets"
msgstr[0] "ゲームセット(アルケルク)"

#. ~ Description of "alquerque set"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid ""
"A wooden box containing all the pieces needed to play a game of alquerque, "
"and also a extremely small guide of how to play it.  In the start, each "
"player places their twelve pieces in the two rows closest to them and in the"
" two rightmost spaces in the center row.  The game is played in turns, with "
"one player taking white and the other black.  The goal of the game is to "
"eliminate the opponent's pieces."
msgstr ""
"木箱の中に、アルケルクのプレイに必要な全ての駒と、遊び方が書かれた小さな紙が入っています。ゲーム開始時、2人のプレイヤーが白駒と黒駒に分かれ、12個の駒を盤上の自陣2列と中央右端2マスに置きます。手番を交互に進め、相手の駒を全て取った者が勝利します。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "dominoes set"
msgid_plural "dominoes sets"
msgstr[0] "ゲームセット(ドミノ)"

#. ~ Description of "dominoes set"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid ""
"A wooden box containing all the pieces needed to play a game of dominoes.  "
"The pieces of this one are perfectly handmade in light wood."
msgstr "木箱の中に、ドミノのプレイに必要な全ての牌が入っています。牌は木製で軽く、手作りされたもののようです。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "jackstraws set"
msgid_plural "jackstraws sets"
msgstr[0] "ゲームセット(ジャックストロー)"

#. ~ Description of "jackstraws set"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid ""
"A cardboard tube containing exactly 60 pieces in various colors for playing "
"a casual pick-up sticks game, alone or with friends.  The rules and values "
"of each color are printed in the cardboard tube, being the colors light "
"blue, dark blue, red, wine, pink, white, black, light green, dark green, "
"cyan, gray, light brown, dark brown and yellow, each one worth a value in-"
"game."
msgstr ""
"段ボール製の筒の中に、色とりどりのピースが60個入っています。ジャックストローは1人でも大勢でも気軽に遊べるゲームです。ピースは水色、紺色、赤色、ワイン色、ピンク色、白色、黒色、薄緑色、濃緑色、シアン、灰色、薄茶色、濃茶色、黄色があり、筒にそれぞれの色に対応するルールと得点が印刷されています。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "Snakes and Ladders"
msgid_plural "Snakes and Ladders"
msgstr[0] "ゲームセット(蛇と梯子)"

#. ~ Description of "Snakes and Ladders"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid ""
"A fun board game, for two or more players, regarded before the Cataclysm as "
"as a worldwide classic.  It is played on a game board with numbered, gridded"
" squares.  A number of 'ladders' and 'snakes' are pictured on the board, "
"each connecting two specific board squares.  The objective of the game is to"
" navigate one's game piece, according to die rolls, from the start (bottom "
"square) to the finish (top square), helped by climbing ladders but hindered "
"by falling down snakes."
msgstr ""
"大変動以前の世界で名作として親しまれてきた、2人以上で楽しめるボードゲームです。盤上には数字を振ったマス目があり、所々に2つのマス目を繋ぐように「梯子」と「蛇」が描かれています。スタート地点(数字が最も小さいマス)に置いた駒をダイスの出目に従って進め、ゴール地点(数字が最も大きいマス)まで移動させれば勝利です。梯子のマスを通ると先へ進めますが、蛇のマスを通ると後ろへ戻されてしまいます。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "Ludo"
msgid_plural "Ludos"
msgstr[0] "ゲームセット(ルドー)"

#. ~ Description of "Ludo"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid ""
"Ludo is a strategy board game for two to four players, in which the players "
"race their four tokens from start to finish according to the rolls of a "
"single dice."
msgstr "ルドーは2人から4人で遊べる戦略ゲームです。サイコロの出目に従って、4つの駒をスタートからゴールまで移動させます。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "Pop-up Pirate"
msgid_plural "Pop-up Pirates"
msgstr[0] "ゲームセット(黒ひげ危機一発)"

#. ~ Description of "Pop-up Pirate"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid ""
"It was once a popular luck-based game.  The pirate is placed into a spring-"
"loaded barrel and rotated to randomize the unlucky slot.  Players must take "
"it in turns to insert plastic swords into slots in the side of the barrel.  "
"If a player inserts the sword into a specific slot (which changes randomly "
"every time the game is played), the pirate is launched out of the barrel and"
" the player is eliminated.  The last player remaining after all others have "
"been eliminated wins."
msgstr ""
"かつての世界で人気が高かった運試しゲームです。バネ仕掛けが付いた樽に海賊人形を入れて回転させ、当たりのスイッチをランダムな位置に移動させます。プレイヤーは、樽の側面に空いている穴のどこか一か所に、プラスチック製の剣を差し込みます。(毎回位置がランダムに変わる)当たりの穴に剣を差し込むと、海賊が樽から飛び出し、そのプレイヤーは脱落します。最後まで残ったプレイヤーが勝利者です。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "Ambuscade!"
msgid_plural "Ambuscade!"
msgstr[0] "ゲームセット(アンブッシュ！)"

#. ~ Description of "Ambuscade!"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid ""
"A fun man-to-man board wargame.  It can be played completely alone or with "
"friends, where when playing alone, the game scenario itself controls the "
"opponent, via tables, charts and a 'paragraph book' which the player refer "
"to see how the opponent is reacting."
msgstr ""
"一対一でも一人でも遊べる、楽しい戦争ゲームです。一人で遊ぶときは、表とグラフ、そして「パラグラフブック」を使って相手の行動を決めながらシナリオを進めます。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "Patrol Leader"
msgid_plural "Patrol Leader"
msgstr[0] "ゲームセット(パトロールリーダー)"

#. ~ Description of "Patrol Leader"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid ""
"Patrol Leader is a tactical solitaire board game.  Is this game, the player "
"is put in the role of a patrol leader in different modern battlefield "
"scenarios, performing missions, capturing or killing enemies, protecting its"
" teammates and advancing in the map.  Very accurate and realistic, "
"guaranteed fun if you like board games."
msgstr ""
"パトロールリーダーは1人用の戦術ゲームです。プレイヤーはシナリオに描かれた様々な現代の戦場で斥候部隊のリーダーとなり、ミッションを遂行し、敵を捕獲または殺害し、仲間を守り、マップ上を前進します。非常に緻密でリアリティが高く、ボードゲーム好きであれば間違いなく楽しめます。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "War Tanks"
msgid_plural "War Tanks"
msgstr[0] "ゲームセット(ウォータンクス)"

#. ~ Description of "War Tanks"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid ""
"War Tanks is a tactical solitaire board game.  In this game, the player "
"control a platoon of tanks in 6 different, fun scenarios, where in the map "
"there are events markers.  When the player moves a tank to a point on the "
"map that has clear line of sight to an event marker, then the player uses "
"the mission cartridge in the cartridge reader to see if there is a paragraph"
" number.  If there is, the player reads the relevant paragraph, which "
"activates one or more enemy units.  Once combat is finished, the player "
"continues to the next event marker, and each scenario outlines how the "
"player accumulates victory points, and how many points are required to "
"declare victory."
msgstr ""
"ウォータンクスは1人用の戦術ゲームです。プレイヤーは楽しい6種類のシナリオの中で、戦車小隊を操作して遊びます。マップ上のイベントマーカーが見える位置まで駒を移動させ、カートリッジリーダーとミッションカートリッジを使って番号を確認します。番号が書いてあった場合はその段落番号の内容を読み、指示に従って敵のユニットを1つ以上置きます。一つの戦闘が終了すると、プレイヤーは次のイベントマーカーに向けて駒を進めます。プレイヤーがポイントを得られる条件や、勝利に必要なポイント数は、各シナリオによって異なります。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "Warships"
msgid_plural "sets of Warships"
msgstr[0] "ゲームセット(レーダー戦術ゲーム)"

#. ~ Description of "Warships"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid ""
"A game where players try to guess where the opponent placed their ships on "
"the board."
msgstr "対戦相手がどのマスに艦の駒を置いたのか推理するゲームです。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "Murder Mystery"
msgid_plural "sets of Murder Mystery"
msgstr[0] "ゲームセット(マーダーミステリー)"

#. ~ Description of "Murder Mystery"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "A game where players try to figure out who murdered the butler."
msgstr "執事を殺した犯人を推理するゲームです。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "key"
msgid_plural "keys"
msgstr[0] "鍵"

#. ~ Description of "key"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid ""
"This is an old nondescript North American Cylinder key.  Lord knows what "
"lock it goes to; best not to bother with it."
msgstr "何の特徴もない、北米で流通しているシリンダー錠用の古びた鍵です。どこの錠を開けられるかなんて、神にしか分かりません。気にするだけ無駄です。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "cigar cutter"
msgid_plural "cigar cutters"
msgstr[0] "シガーカッター"

#. ~ Description of "cigar cutter"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid ""
"A set of small blades that pinch together to cut the end off of a cigar."
msgstr "葉巻の先端をカットするための、小さな刃が付いた道具です。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "cigar punch"
msgid_plural "cigar punches"
msgstr[0] "シガーパンチ"

#. ~ Description of "cigar punch"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "A small tube meant to cut a hole in the end of a cigar."
msgstr "葉巻の先端に穴をあけるための、小さな筒状の道具です。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "portable seismograph"
msgid_plural "portable seismographs"
msgstr[0] "携帯型地震計"

#. ~ Description of "portable seismograph"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid ""
"A sturdy steel briefcase, containing what appears to be an old-fashioned drum seismograph.  The stenciled acronyms of its outer case imply it was used by XEDRA as some sort of recording device.\n"
"\n"
"Thin parallel lines cover both ends of the drum, but as they approach the middle their vibrations intensify, until the ink fuses into thick red stain."
msgstr ""
"昔ながらの地震計に似た円筒形の装置が入った、頑丈な鋼鉄製のブリーフケースです。ケース表面にステンシルされた英字を見れば、この装置を使ってXEDRAが何らかの記録を取っていたことが分かります。\n"
"\n"
"円筒の表面には細い2本の線が平行に走っていますが、記録の中程で振動が激しくなったのか鮮やかな赤いインクの染みができています。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "NRE microphone"
msgid_plural "NRE microphones"
msgstr[0] "NREマイク"

#. ~ Description of "NRE microphone"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid ""
"A squat tripod supports what appears to be a rather long microphone encased "
"within a glass ampoule.  You can't tell whether it's meant to record audio, "
"or something else entirely."
msgstr ""
"ガラスに包まれた長いマイクのような装置がずんぐりとした三脚の先端に付いています。これが録音装置なのか、それとも何かまったく別のものを記録する装置なのかは分かりません。"

#. ~ Description of "incense"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "A small rod giving off a nice smell."
msgstr "いい香りがする細い棒です。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "writ of trade"
msgid_plural "writs of trade"
msgstr[0] "取引契約書"

#. ~ Description of "writ of trade"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid ""
"A short writ featuring the signed agreement of establishing a trade route."
msgstr "交易ルートを開設することを約束した、サイン入りの簡単な契約書です。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid "laboratory shipping records"
msgid_plural "laboratory shipping records"
msgstr[0] "研究所出荷記録"

#. ~ Description of "laboratory shipping records"
#: data/json/items/fluff.json
msgid ""
"Some type of advanced data storage device, filled with logistical data on "
"subterranean train routes and schedules."
msgstr "地下鉄のルートやダイヤといった物流データが記録された、高度なデータ記憶装置です。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fuel.json
msgid "ethanol"
msgid_plural "ethanol"
msgstr[0] "エタノール"

#. ~ Description of "ethanol"
#: data/json/items/fuel.json
msgid ""
"Extremely pure alcohol suitable for use as a component in chemical "
"reactions.  You could also water it down and drink it, or use it as fuel in "
"alcohol-burning stoves."
msgstr "高純度のアルコールです。化学反応の素材に適しており、水で割って飲む事も出来ます。また、アルコールストーブの燃料としても使えます。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fuel.json
msgid "methylated spirits"
msgid_plural "methylated spirits"
msgstr[0] "変性エタノール"

#. ~ Description of "methylated spirits"
#: data/json/items/fuel.json
msgid ""
"A high-strength ethanol solution mixed with methanol to make it toxic to "
"drink, so as to avoid pre-apocalyptic regulations on ethanol.  Intended for "
"use in alcohol-burning stoves and as a solvent."
msgstr ""
"毒性があり、飲食用に転用される事を防ぐ為にメタノールを混合した高強度のエタノール溶液です。溶剤やアルコールストーブの燃料に使う事を想定しています。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fuel.json
msgid "denatured alcohol"
msgid_plural "denatured alcohols"
msgstr[0] "変性アルコール"

#. ~ Description of "denatured alcohol"
#: data/json/items/fuel.json
msgid ""
"A high-strength ethanol solution mixed with denatonium benzoate to make it "
"impossibly bitter to drink, so as to avoid pre-apocalyptic regulations on "
"ethanol.  Intended for use in alcohol-burning stoves and as a solvent."
msgstr ""
"大変動以前のエタノール規制を避ける目的で生まれた、高純度エタノール溶液に苦い安息香酸デナトニウムを混ぜて飲用に適さない状態にした液体です。アルコールストーブや溶剤として使うことが想定されています。"

#. ~ Description of "methanol"
#: data/json/items/fuel.json
msgid ""
"High purity methanol suitable for use in chemical reactions.  Could be used "
"in alcohol-burning stoves.  Very toxic."
msgstr "化学反応での使用に適した高純度メタノールです。アルコールを燃焼させるストーブで利用できます。強い毒性があります。"

#. ~ Description of "diesel"
#: data/json/items/fuel.json
msgid ""
"Petroleum-based fuel made from a byproduct of the gasoline making process."
msgstr "ガソリンの精製過程で得られる副産物の一種です。主にディーゼルエンジンの燃料として用いられます。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fuel.json
msgid "JP8 fuel"
msgid_plural "JP8 fuel"
msgstr[0] "JP-8燃料"

#. ~ Description of "JP8 fuel"
#: data/json/items/fuel.json
msgid ""
"A kerosene-based fuel used mainly by US military vehicles as a replacement "
"for diesel and jet fuel, to simplify logistics."
msgstr "灯油を主成分とする燃料です。兵站の簡素化を図るために、主に軍用車両で軽油やジェット燃料の代替として使われています。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fuel.json
msgid "avgas fuel"
msgid_plural "avgas fuel"
msgstr[0] "航空燃料"

#. ~ Description of "avgas fuel"
#: data/json/items/fuel.json
msgid "A specialized type of petroleum-based fuel used to power aircraft."
msgstr "航空機の動力源として使われる、特殊な石油系燃料です。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fuel.json
msgid "biodiesel"
msgid_plural "biodiesel"
msgstr[0] "バイオディーゼル"

#. ~ Description of "biodiesel"
#: data/json/items/fuel.json
msgid ""
"Vegetable oil- or animal fat-based diesel fuel consisting of long-chain "
"alkyl (methyl, ethyl, or propyl) esters."
msgstr "長鎖アルキル(メチル、エチル、またはプロピル)エステルを含む、植物油、あるいは動物脂肪を原料とした軽油です。"

#. ~ Description of "gasoline"
#: data/json/items/fuel.json
msgid ""
"Gasoline is a highly flammable liquid.  When under pressure, it has the "
"potential for violent explosion."
msgstr "ガソリンは可燃性の高い液体です。圧力が掛かると大爆発を起こす可能性があります。"

#. ~ Description of "kerosene"
#: data/json/items/fuel.json
msgid "A thin and clean-burning oil made for use in oil lamps."
msgstr "オイルランプ用に作られた薄く綺麗なオイルです。"

#. ~ Description of "motor oil"
#: data/json/items/fuel.json
msgid "An oil made for use in car engines."
msgstr "自動車のエンジンで使われるオイルです。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fuel.json
msgid "napalm"
msgid_plural "napalm"
msgstr[0] "ナパーム"

#. ~ Description of "napalm"
#: data/json/items/fuel.json
msgid ""
"This is gasoline mixed with some other components to make it stick to the "
"surface and increase burning temperature, meant to be used with a "
"flamethrower."
msgstr "ガソリンに複数の素材を混合し、ある程度の粘性を持たせ、燃焼温度を高めました。火炎放射器に最適です。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fuel.json
msgid "gelled gasoline"
msgid_plural "gelled gasoline"
msgstr[0] "ゲル化ガソリン"

#. ~ Description of "gelled gasoline"
#: data/json/items/fuel.json
msgid ""
"A flammable gel composed of gasoline and dissolved shavings of polystyrene, "
"roughly similar in properties to napalm B.  It's meant to be used with a "
"flamethrower."
msgstr "ガソリンにポリスチレン切削物を溶融させた可燃性のゲルです。ナパームBと似た性質を示します。つまり、火炎放射器の燃料に使えるということです。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fuel.json
msgid "flamethrower fuel"
msgid_plural "flamethrower fuel"
msgstr[0] "火炎放射器燃料"

#. ~ Description of "flamethrower fuel"
#: data/json/items/fuel.json
msgid ""
"A mixture of gasoline and diesel oil in equal parts.  Its combustion "
"properties make it unfit for applications where you would use any of them "
"separately, but it can be used to feed a flamethrower."
msgstr ""
"ガソリンとディーゼルオイルを同比率で混合した液体です。燃焼効率はそれぞれを単独で燃やした場合に到底及びませんが、火炎放射器の燃料として利用できます。"

#. ~ Density of propane gas at 25C is 1.808 kg/m3, liquid propane at 25C is
#. 0.493 g/cm3, propane tanks are pressurized enough to turn it liquid.
#. ~ Description of "propane"
#: data/json/items/fuel.json
msgid ""
"Propane gas, useful for everything from torches to barbeque grills to "
"metalworking."
msgstr "バーナー、バーベキューグリル、金属加工などあらゆる用途に使えるプロパンガスです。"

#. ~ Description of "turpentine"
#: data/json/items/fuel.json
msgid "Oil of turpentine, distilled from pine resin or crude oil."
msgstr "松脂や原油から蒸留したテレビン油です。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/fuel.json
msgid "camphine"
msgid_plural "camphine"
msgstr[0] "カンフェン"

#. ~ Description of "camphine"
#: data/json/items/fuel.json
msgid ""
"A blend of turpentine and ethanol, historically used as the successor to "
"whale oil for lamps before kerosene."
msgstr "テレビン油とエタノールの混合物です。かつては鯨油の代替品としてランプの燃料に使われていました。"

#. ~ Description of "crude lamp oil"
#: data/json/items/fuel.json
msgid "A crude, natural oil made for use in pre-modern oil lamps."
msgstr "近代以前のオイルランプに使われていた天然油です。"

#. ~ pseudo item, used as fuel type for engines that are animal-powered
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "animal"
msgid_plural "animal"
msgstr[0] "動物"

#. ~ pseudo item, only used for crafting as a required tool
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "nearby fire"
msgid_plural "nearby fire"
msgstr[0] "火元"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "cottonwood tree boll"
msgid_plural "cottonwood tree bolls"
msgstr[0] "ポプラの綿毛"

#. ~ Description of "cottonwood tree boll"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"A fluffy white seed.  While it looks like the common cotton, it is too weak "
"and short to be turned into clothing."
msgstr "フワフワの綿毛が付いた種子です。綿の実によく似ていますが、衣服を作るには強度と長さが足りません。"

#. ~ pseudo item, used as fuel type for engines that are human-powered
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "muscle"
msgid_plural "muscle"
msgstr[0] "筋肉"

#. ~ pseudo item, used as fuel type for engines that are wind-powered
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "wind"
msgid_plural "wind"
msgstr[0] "風"

#. ~ pseudo item, used as fuel type for CBMs that are sun-powered
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "sun light"
msgid_plural "sun light"
msgstr[0] "太陽光"

#. ~ pseudo item, used as fuel type for CBMs that are metabolism-powered
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "metabolism"
msgid_plural "metabolisms"
msgstr[0] "代謝"

#. ~ pseudo item, only used for as a required tool, checked for in
#. player::amount_of
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "a smoking device and a source of flame"
msgid_plural "a smoking device and a source of flame"
msgstr[0] "喫煙道具と着火道具"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "file"
msgid_plural "files"
msgstr[0] "ファイル"

#. ~ Description of "file"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"Several documents with all kinds of information, customer data and charts "
"kept together, pretty useless now though."
msgstr "図表や顧客データ等の文書が入ったファイルです。今となっては何の役にも立たないでしょう。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "INCIDENT REPORT: IMMERSION-27A"
msgid_plural "INCIDENT REPORT: IMMERSION-27As"
msgstr[0] "事故報告: 次元浸入-27A"

#. ~ Description of "INCIDENT REPORT: IMMERSION-27A"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"A white piece of paper, with the logo of XEDRA printed on its upper left "
"corner.  It seems to be an internal report of some kind."
msgstr "左上にXEDRAのロゴが印字された白い紙です。何らかの内部報告書のようです。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "MATERIAL: T-SUBSTRATE"
msgid_plural "MATERIAL: T-SUBSTRATEs"
msgstr[0] "素材: 基質T"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "HAADF MICROGRAPH: T-SUBSTRATE"
msgid_plural "HAADF MICROGRAPH: T-SUBSTRATEs"
msgstr[0] "HAADF像: 基質T"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "XEDRA document"
msgid_plural "XEDRA documents"
msgstr[0] "XEDRA文書"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "ANOMALOUS ARTIFACT REPORT"
msgid_plural "ANOMALOUS ARTIFACT REPORTs"
msgstr[0] "異常アーティファクト記録"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "short NRE printout"
msgid_plural "short NRE printouts"
msgstr[0] "NRE印刷データS"

#. ~ Description of "short NRE printout"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"A sequence of overlapping numbers plotted in thermal paper, at times so "
"densely packed that they disappear into thick blots of oxide colored ink.  A"
" few number sequences repeat in an almost orderly fashion, but you can't "
"tell whether that means anything."
msgstr ""
"感熱紙に並んだ数字の列は、一部の印字がぼやけて読み取りにくくなるほど密集しています。何度も繰り返し記されている数列もあるようですが、それが何を意味しているのかはよく分かりません。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "NRE printout"
msgid_plural "NRE printouts"
msgstr[0] "NRE印刷データM"

#. ~ Description of "NRE printout"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"A long sequence of overlapping numbers plotted in thermal paper, at times so"
" densely packed that they disappear into thick blots of oxide colored ink.  "
"Blots and numbers appear to be arranged in a strangely pleasing pattern."
msgstr ""
"感熱紙に並んだ数字の長い列は、一部の印字がぼやけて読み取りにくくなるほど密集しています。ぼやけた印字と数字の羅列が奇妙で美しい紋様を形作っているように見えます。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "long NRE printout"
msgid_plural "long NRE printouts"
msgstr[0] "NRE印刷データL"

#. ~ Description of "long NRE printout"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"A very, very long sequence of overlapping numbers plotted in thermal paper."
"  It is almost 15 feet long."
msgstr "約4.5mというとんでもない長さの感熱紙に、長大な数列が密集して印字されています"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "Foodplace loyalty card"
msgid_plural "Foodplace loyalty cards"
msgstr[0] "フードプレイスポイントカード"

#. ~ Description of "Foodplace loyalty card"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"A bright pink loyalty card, all the points are stamped.  This would "
"definitely prove your fidelity to Foodplace, if it still meant anything…"
msgstr "全てのスタンプが押された、鮮やかなピンク色のポイントカードです。フードプレイスへの忠誠心を示す以外の使い道が残っているとは思えません..."

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "twig"
msgid_plural "twigs"
msgstr[0] "小枝"

#. ~ Description of "twig"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"A small and slender branch.  Makes passable firewood but is not useful for "
"much else."
msgstr "小さな細い枝です、焚き木にはなりますが、それ以外の使い道はあまりありません。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "handful of leaves"
msgid_plural "handfuls of leaves"
msgstr[0] "葉"

#. ~ Description of "handful of leaves"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"Some ordinary, mostly dry leaves.  They have very few uses and are thus "
"(almost) only good for burning."
msgstr "生きた葉や枯れ葉です。焚き付けにはなりますが、それ以外の使い道は(ほとんど)ありません。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "withered plant"
msgid_plural "withered plants"
msgstr[0] "枯れた植物"

#. ~ Description of "withered plant"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"A dead plant.  Good for starting fires or making crude tailoring crafts."
msgstr "枯れた植物です。焚き付けにする、簡単な工芸品の材料にするなどの使い道があります。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "superglue"
msgid_plural "superglue"
msgstr[0] "瞬間接着剤"

#. ~ Description of "superglue"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "A tube of strong glue.  Used in many crafting recipes."
msgstr "チューブに入った強力な接着剤です。多くのレシピで利用します。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "rubber cement"
msgid_plural "rubber cement"
msgstr[0] "ゴム用接着剤"

#. ~ Description of "rubber cement"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"A tin of adhesive typically used to glue rubber.  It forms a less rigid bond"
" than typical superglue making it ideal for projects requiring flexibility."
"  Typically smelly and toxic."
msgstr ""
"ゴムの接着に用いる、缶入りの接着剤です。一般的な瞬間接着剤と比べて接着力は弱まりますが、柔軟性を必要とする部品の接着に適しています。酷い臭いと毒性は我慢しましょう。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "bone glue"
msgid_plural "bone glues"
msgstr[0] "膠"

#. ~ Description of "bone glue"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"Glue made from boiling animal bones.  The adhesive isn't strong enough for "
"heavy-duty usages, but it can be used as a varnish or holding together small"
" items."
msgstr "骨を煮詰めて作った接着剤です。接着力はそれほど強くありませんが、小さな物同士をくっつけるには十分です。ワニスとしても使用できます。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "fertilizer"
msgid_plural "fertilizers"
msgstr[0] "肥料"

#. ~ Description of "fertilizer"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "A token representing fertilization of a plant."
msgstr "植物に肥料を与えたことを示す代用アイテムです。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "steel chain"
msgid_plural "steel chains"
msgstr[0] "チェーン"

#. ~ Description of "steel chain"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"A heavy steel chain.  Useful as a weapon, or for crafting.  It has a chance "
"to wrap around your target, allowing for a bonus unarmed attack."
msgstr "厚鋼製の鎖です。武器にもアイテムの製作にも使えます。この武器は攻撃目標に絡まる可能性があり、素手による攻撃にボーナスを見込めます。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "chunk of chitin"
msgid_plural "chunks of chitin"
msgstr[0] "キチンの塊"

#. ~ Description of "chunk of chitin"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "A piece of an insect's exoskeleton.  It is light and very durable."
msgstr "昆虫の外骨格の一部です。軽くて非常に耐久性があります。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "strand of endochitin"
msgid_plural "strands of endochitin"
msgstr[0] "体内キチン"

#. ~ Description of "strand of endochitin"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "A piece of an insect's endoskeleton."
msgstr "昆虫の内骨格の一部です。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json data/mods/Aftershock/items/alien_organics.json
msgid "cluster of gas sacs"
msgid_plural "clusters of gas sacs"
msgstr[0] "ガス嚢"

#. ~ Description of "cluster of gas sacs"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"This is a cluster of membranous bubbles, each about the size of a grape, "
"retrieved from inside a mutant insect.  They float like tiny helium balloons"
" - perhaps they are full of a lighter-than-air gas."
msgstr ""
"変異した昆虫の体内から採取した、ブドウほどの大きさの泡状の膜の集合体です。膜の中には空気より軽いガスが入っているのか、小さなヘリウム気球のように浮かんでいます。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "ballast organs"
msgid_plural "clusters of ballast organs"
msgstr[0] "囲心腔"

#. ~ Description of "ballast organs"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"This is a cluster of hydrostatic organs, each about the size of a baseball, "
"retrieved from inside a kraken mutant.  Some of them seem to be lighter than"
" air, and some seem to weigh as much as air."
msgstr ""
"クラーケンと呼ばれる変異体の体内から採取された、野球ボールほどの大きさの静水圧器官です。空気より軽いものや、空気と同じ重さのものなど、重量は様々です。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "chunk of biosilicified chitin"
msgid_plural "chunks of biosilicified chitin"
msgstr[0] "シリコンキチン塊"

#. ~ Description of "chunk of biosilicified chitin"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"A lump of exoskeleton that has undergone biosilicification.  It is acid-"
"resistant but rather brittle."
msgstr "シリコン化した生物の外骨格です。耐酸性に優れているものの、耐久性に不安があります。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "bundle of cotton patches"
msgid_plural "bundles of cotton patches"
msgstr[0] "資材束(綿端切れ)"

#. ~ Description of "bundle of cotton patches"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"Cotton patches, bundled tightly together for storage.  Disassemble to "
"unpack."
msgstr "保管のためにしっかりと束ねた綿の端切れです。分解して使いましょう。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "bundle of cotton sheets"
msgid_plural "bundles of cotton sheets"
msgstr[0] "資材束(綿生地)"

#. ~ Description of "bundle of cotton sheets"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"Cotton sheets, bundled tightly together for storage.  Disassemble to unpack."
msgstr "保管のためにしっかりと束ねた綿の生地です。分解して使いましょう。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "bundle of leather"
msgid_plural "bundles of leather"
msgstr[0] "資材束(革端切れ)"

#. ~ Description of "bundle of leather"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"Leather patches, bundled tightly together for storage.  Disassemble to "
"unpack."
msgstr "保管のためにしっかりと束ねた革の端切れです。分解して使いましょう。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "bundle of felt"
msgid_plural "bundles of felt"
msgstr[0] "資材束(ﾌｪﾙﾄ端切れ)"

#. ~ Description of "bundle of felt"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"Felt patches, bundled tightly together for storage.  Disassemble to unpack."
msgstr "保管のためにしっかりと束ねたフェルトの端切れです。分解して使いましょう。"

#. ~ total volume is equal to 10 planks, assuming uniformity and tight
#. stacking
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "bundle of planks"
msgid_plural "bundles of planks"
msgstr[0] "資材束(木材)"

#. ~ total volume is equal to 10 planks, assuming uniformity and tight
#. stacking
#. ~ Description of "bundle of planks"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"Ten construction planks securely tied together for easier transport.  "
"Disassemble to untie them."
msgstr "10枚の建設用木材をロープで固定し、持ち運びやすくしたものです。分解するとロープを解きます。"

#. ~ total volume is equal to 10 rebars, assuming uniformity and tight
#. stacking
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "bundle of rebars"
msgid_plural "bundles of rebars"
msgstr[0] "資材束(鉄筋)"

#. ~ total volume is equal to 10 rebars, assuming uniformity and tight
#. stacking
#. ~ Description of "bundle of rebars"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"Ten pieces of rebar securely tied together for easier transport.  "
"Disassemble to untie them."
msgstr "10本の鉄筋ををロープで固定し、持ち運びやすくしたものです。分解するとロープを解きます。"

#. ~ total volume is equal to 10 pipes, assuming uniformity and tight stacking
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "bundle of pipes"
msgid_plural "bundles of pipes"
msgstr[0] "資材束(パイプ)"

#. ~ total volume is equal to 10 pipes, assuming uniformity and tight stacking
#. ~ Description of "bundle of pipes"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"Ten pipes securely tied together for easier transport.  Disassemble to untie"
" them."
msgstr "10本のパイプをロープで固定し、持ち運びやすくしたものです。分解するとロープを解きます。"

#. ~ total volume is equal to 10 pipes, assuming uniformity and tight stacking
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "bundle of copper tubing"
msgid_plural "bundles of copper tubing"
msgstr[0] "資材束(銅管)"

#. ~ total volume is equal to 10 pipes, assuming uniformity and tight stacking
#. ~ Description of "bundle of copper tubing"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"Ten copper pipes securely tied together for easier transport.  Disassemble "
"to untie them."
msgstr "10本の銅管をロープで固定し、持ち運びやすくしたものです。分解するとロープを解きます。"

#. ~ total volume is greater than 10 sticks; irregular dimensions leave air
#. gaps
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "bundle of sticks"
msgid_plural "bundles of sticks"
msgstr[0] "資材束(棒)"

#. ~ total volume is greater than 10 sticks; irregular dimensions leave air
#. gaps
#. ~ Description of "bundle of sticks"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"Ten sticks securely tied together for easier transport.  Disassemble to "
"untie them."
msgstr "10本の棒をロープで固定し、持ち運びやすくしたものです。分解するとロープを解きます。"

#. ~ total volume is greater than 5 long sticks, since they are rough lumber
#. and do not stack perfectly
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "bundle of long sticks"
msgid_plural "bundles of long sticks"
msgstr[0] "資材束(長棒)"

#. ~ total volume is greater than 5 long sticks, since they are rough lumber
#. and do not stack perfectly
#. ~ Description of "bundle of long sticks"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"Five long sticks securely tied together for easier transport.  Disassemble "
"to untie them."
msgstr "5本の長棒をロープで固定し、持ち運びやすくしたものです。分解するとロープを解きます。"

#. ~ total volume is greater than 5 wooden javelins, since they are rough
#. lumber and do not stack perfectly
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "bundle of javelins"
msgid_plural "bundles of javelins"
msgstr[0] "資材束(ジャベリン)"

#. ~ total volume is greater than 5 wooden javelins, since they are rough
#. lumber and do not stack perfectly
#. ~ Description of "bundle of javelins"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"Five wooden javelins securely tied together for easier transport.  "
"Disassemble to untie them."
msgstr "5本の木製ジャベリンをロープで固定し、持ち運びやすくしたものです。分解するとロープを解きます。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "t-substrate sample"
msgid_plural "t-substrate samples"
msgstr[0] "基質T"

#. ~ Description of "t-substrate sample"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"An acrylic cube cast around a small black crystal.  It's tepid to the touch."
msgstr "小さな黒い結晶の周囲を透明な立方体が回っています。ほのかな熱を感じます。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "biollante bud"
msgid_plural "biollante buds"
msgstr[0] "ビオランテの蕾"

#. ~ Description of "biollante bud"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"An unopened biollante flower, brilliant purple in color.  It may still have "
"its sap-producing organ intact."
msgstr "まだ開いていないビオランテの花です。鮮やかな紫色が目を引きます。樹液を作る器官がそのまま残されています。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "empty canister"
msgid_plural "empty canisters"
msgstr[0] "空円筒弾"

#. ~ Description of "empty canister"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"An empty canister, which may have once held tear gas or other substances."
msgstr "空の円筒形の容器です。催涙ガスなど色々な物質を内部に充填できます。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "petrified eye"
msgid_plural "petrified eyes"
msgstr[0] "石化した眼"

#. ~ Description of "petrified eye"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"A fist-sized eyeball with a cross-shaped pupil.  It seems to be made of "
"stone, but doesn't look like it was carved."
msgstr "十字型の瞳孔をもった拳ほどのサイズの眼球です。素材は石のようですが、人の手で彫られたようには見えません。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "spiral stone"
msgid_plural "spiral stones"
msgstr[0] "螺旋状の石"

#. ~ Description of "spiral stone"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"A rock the size of your fist.  It is covered with intricate spirals; it is "
"impossible to tell whether they are carved, naturally formed, or some kind "
"of fossil."
msgstr ""
"拳ほどの大きさの石です。螺旋状の複雑な模様が浮き出ています。人の手が加えられているのか、自然にそうなっているのか、はたまた何かの化石なのかは分かりません。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "USB drive"
msgid_plural "USB drives"
msgstr[0] "USBメモリ"

#. ~ Description of "USB drive"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "A USB thumb drive.  Useful for holding software."
msgstr "ソフトウェアの保存に便利なUSBメモリです。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "secured USB drive"
msgid_plural "secured USB drives"
msgstr[0] "耐衝撃USBメモリ"

#. ~ Description of "secured USB drive"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"A USB thumb drive.  Useful for holding software.  This one seems like it "
"could get ran over by a truck and be fine."
msgstr "ソフトウェアの保存に便利なUSBメモリです。トラックに轢かれても壊れそうにありません。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "DARPA hard case"
msgid_plural "DARPA hard cases"
msgstr[0] "DARPAハードケース"

#. ~ Description of "DARPA hard case"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"A heavy and very durable protective case made of steel and thick plastic, "
"locked with a six dials.  A sticker with the logo of DARPA is attached to "
"the front, but looking at the surface, you can see that another marking - "
"formerly stenciled into the material - was recently and hastily destroyed."
msgstr ""
"スチールと厚いプラスチックでできた、非常に頑丈で重い保護ケースです。6つのダイヤルが付いており、ロックされています。前面のDARPAのロゴ入りステッカーをよく見ると、元々付いていた何かのマークを急いで消したような痕跡が残っています。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "FEMA data"
msgid_plural "FEMA data"
msgstr[0] "FEMAデータ"

#. ~ Description of "FEMA data"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"Evacuation plans, disaster risk projections, personnel lists and last minute"
" communications from just before the end, all scrubbed from FEMA servers and"
" stored in an external hdd."
msgstr ""
"FEMAサーバーから抽出された避難計画、災害リスク予測、人員リスト、世界崩壊直前の通信記録などのあらゆるデータが、この外付けHDDに保存されています。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "candlestick"
msgid_plural "candlesticks"
msgstr[0] "燭台"

#. ~ Description of "candlestick"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "A gold candlestick."
msgstr "金製の燭台です。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "chalice"
msgid_plural "chalices"
msgstr[0] "盃"

#. ~ Description of "chalice"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "A gold chalice."
msgstr "金製の盃です。"

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Vehicle part name
#: data/json/items/generic.json data/json/vehicleparts/vehicle_parts.json
msgid "blade"
msgid_plural "blades"
msgstr[0] "刃"

#. ~ Description of "blade"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"A large, relatively sharp blade.  Could be used to make bladed weaponry, or "
"attached to a car."
msgstr "比較的鋭い大きな刃です。斬撃武器の製作や車両に取り付けて使用できます。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "scythe blade"
msgid_plural "scythe blades"
msgstr[0] "湾曲刃"

#. ~ Description of "scythe blade"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"A large, curved blade.  Could be used to assemble a scythe, or make an "
"improvised polearm."
msgstr "湾曲した大きな刃です。鎌や即席武器の材料として利用できます。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "circular sawblade"
msgid_plural "circular sawblades"
msgstr[0] "丸ノコギリ刃"

#. ~ Description of "circular sawblade"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"An 8\" circular sawblade.  You could make a saw with it, or throw it.  "
"Wielding it without sturdy gloves is a bad idea."
msgstr ""
"外径8インチの丸ノコギリ刃です。工具に取り付けてもいいですし、武器として投擲しても構いません。丈夫なグローブなしで扱うのは止めた方がよさそうです。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "tree spile"
msgid_plural "tree spiles"
msgstr[0] "差し管"

#. ~ Description of "tree spile"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"A hollow metal cylinder which is inserted in a tree crust in order to slowly"
" harvest its sap.  Can be used on a maple tree in between late winter and "
"early spring to harvest maple sap."
msgstr ""
"木の皮に差し入れて樹液を採取するための、金属製シリンダーです。冬の終わりから春の初めにかけて、カエデの木に使用することで樹液を採取できます。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "wire"
msgid_plural "wires"
msgstr[0] "ワイヤー"

#. ~ Description of "wire"
#. ~ Description of "mild steel wire"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"A length of thin, relatively stiff, steel wire.  Like the sort you find in "
"wire fences."
msgstr "細長く比較的硬い鋼のワイヤーです。フェンスにも使われている素材です。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "mild steel wire"
msgid_plural "mild steel wires"
msgstr[0] "ワイヤー(低炭素鋼)"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "medium steel wire"
msgid_plural "medium steel wires"
msgstr[0] "ワイヤー(中炭素鋼)"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "high steel wire"
msgid_plural "high steel wires"
msgstr[0] "ワイヤー(高炭素鋼)"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "hardened steel wire"
msgid_plural "hardened steel wires"
msgstr[0] "ワイヤー(焼入炭素鋼)"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "tempered steel wire"
msgid_plural "tempered steel wires"
msgstr[0] "ワイヤー(焼戻炭素鋼)"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "barbed wire"
msgid_plural "barbed wires"
msgstr[0] "有刺鉄線"

#. ~ Description of "barbed wire"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "A length of stiff wire, covered in sharp barbs."
msgstr "鋭い棘に覆われた硬く長いワイヤーです。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "steel mesh"
msgid_plural "steel meshes"
msgstr[0] "金網"

#. ~ Description of "steel mesh"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"A mat of woven fine steel wire, useful for dryer lint traps and reusable "
"coffee filter baskets.  You could put these on a window to keep mosquitoes "
"and other bugs out, but chain link fencing will do these days."
msgstr ""
"乾燥機の糸くずフィルターやコーヒーフィルターなどに利用できる、鋼鉄ワイヤー製の目が細かい網です。窓にはめ込んで蚊などの虫の侵入を防ぐことも可能ですが、今の状況ならもっと目の粗い柵でも代用できますね。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "rebar"
msgid_plural "rebars"
msgstr[0] "鉄筋"

#. ~ Description of "rebar"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"A length of rebar, makes a nice melee weapon, and could be handy in "
"constructing tougher walls and such."
msgstr "鉄筋です。武器として使えます。壁などの建造物の補強に重宝します。"

#. ~ Description of "small railroad track"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "A length of track, made from some planks and rails."
msgstr "厚板とレールで作られた鉄道レールです。"

#. ~ Description of "concrete"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "Some concrete, ready to be used in a construction project."
msgstr "いつでも建築に使えるよう調整されたコンクリートです。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "bone skewer"
msgid_plural "bone skewers"
msgstr[0] "骨串"

#. ~ Description of "bone skewer"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"A thin skewer carved from bone.  Sadly, it won't make squirrel on a stick "
"taste better."
msgstr "骨を削って作った細い串です。残念ながら、これでリスの串焼きを作っても味は向上しません。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "burnt out torch"
msgid_plural "burnt out torches"
msgstr[0] "松明(使用済)"

#. ~ Description of "burnt out torch"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid ""
"A torch that has consumed all its fuel; it can be recrafted into another "
"torch."
msgstr "燃料を使い切った松明です。新しい松明に再利用できます。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "dead flare"
msgid_plural "dead flares"
msgstr[0] "発炎筒(使用済)"

#. ~ Description of "dead flare"
#: data/json/items/generic.json
msgid "This is a spent magnesium flare.  It is essentially trash."
msgstr "使用済みのマグネシウム照明です。使い道のないゴミですね。"

