#. ~ juice pulp is an arbitrary item, but needed some baseline nutrients for
#. byproducts
#. ~ Description of "juice pulp"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A handful of stringy pulp, left-over from juicing some kind of fruit.  It's "
"not very tasty, but contains a lot of healthy fiber."
msgstr "果物を搾ってジュースをした後に残る、繊維質のカスです。あまり美味しくはありませんが、健康にいい食物繊維が多く含まれています。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "pear"
msgid_plural "pears"
msgstr[0] "洋ナシ"

#. ~ Description of "pear"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A juicy, bell-shaped pear.  Yum!"
msgstr "ベルの形をした瑞々しい洋ナシです。美味しいよ！"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "guava"
msgid_plural "guavas"
msgstr[0] "グアバ"

#. ~ Description of "guava"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A sweet, sandy-textured fruit with pink flesh native to the Caribbean, "
"Central America, and South America.  Great for making milkshakes."
msgstr "カリブ海や中南米が原産の、ピンク色の果肉をもつ果実です。ザラつく舌ざわりの甘味はミルクセーキによく合います。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "passionfruit"
msgid_plural "passionfruits"
msgstr[0] "パッションフルーツ"

#. ~ Description of "passionfruit"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A sweet, acidic fruit originating from South America.  It grows on vines and"
" is filled with seeds like a pomegranate.  Also known as the maracuya."
msgstr "南米原産の甘酸っぱい果物です。蔓性の植物に実り、果肉内にはザクロのように種が混じっています。マラクジャという別名でも知られています。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "lulo"
msgid_plural "lulos"
msgstr[0] "ルロ"

#. ~ Description of "lulo"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"An acidic fruit found in South America and the Caribbean, it looks like a "
"hairy orange and is used mainly for juice and desserts.  Also known as the "
"naranjilla."
msgstr ""
"南米やカリブ海諸島に生育している、酸味のある果物です。毛が生えたオレンジのような見た目をしており、主にジュースやデザートの材料に使われます。ナランジラという別名でも知られています。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "grapefruit"
msgid_plural "grapefruits"
msgstr[0] "グレープフルーツ"

#. ~ Description of "grapefruit"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A hybrid citrus fruit descended from the orange, whose taste ranges from "
"sour to semi-sweet, and a little bitter."
msgstr "オレンジに近い柑橘類の交配種です。甘味よりも酸味が強く、多少の苦味があります。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "cherries"
msgid_plural "cherries"
msgstr[0] "サクランボ"

#. ~ Description of "cherries"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A sweet red fruit that grows on trees.  If you have some time on your hands,"
" maybe you could figure out how to do that trick where you tie a knot in the"
" stem with your tongue."
msgstr "木に実る赤い果実です。もし暇で仕方ないなら、舌だけを使って茎を結ぶ技の習得を目指してみるのはどうでしょう。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "plum"
msgid_plural "plums"
msgstr[0] "スモモ"

#. ~ Description of "plum"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A large purple plum.  Tasty and good for your digestion."
msgstr "紫色の大きなスモモです。消化を助ける美味しい果物です。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "grapes"
msgid_plural "grapes"
msgstr[0] "ブドウ"

#. ~ Description of "grapes"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A cluster of juicy grapes.  Quite calorie-dense compared to most fruit, and "
"you might be able to make them into wine if you're ambitious enough."
msgstr "ジューシーなブドウの房です。他の果物に比べるとカロリーが高く、その気になればワインを作れるかもしれません。"

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Plant name of seed "pineapple stem"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/seed.json
msgid "pineapple"
msgid_plural "pineapples"
