#: data/mods/Aftershock/items/seed.json
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/items/comestibles/seed.json
msgid "melon"
msgid_plural "melons"
msgstr[0] "メロン"

#. ~ based on a canteloupe
#. ~ Description of "melon"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A large and very sweet fruit.  Botanically speaking, all melons are actually"
" berries."
msgstr "大きくて非常に甘い果物です。植物学的には、メロンは野菜ではありません。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "blackberries"
msgid_plural "blackberries"
msgstr[0] "ブラックベリー"

#. ~ Description of "blackberries"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A darker cousin of the raspberry.  The color isn't actually what sets them "
"apart - the identifying characteristic is whether the stem stays connected "
"to the fruit when it's first picked."
msgstr ""
"ラズベリーより黒っぽい親戚のようなベリーですが、両者を見分けるポイントは色ではありません。収穫したときに茎が実から簡単に外れなければ、それはブラックベリーです。"

#. ~ serving size is 250 ml of edible material, extra volume is the pit.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "mango"
msgid_plural "mangos"
msgstr[0] "マンゴー"

#. ~ serving size is 250 ml of edible material, extra volume is the pit.
#. ~ Description of "mango"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A fleshy tropical fruit with a large pit.  Better enjoy it soon, you're "
"pretty sure more of these aren't going to be imported for a long time."
msgstr "大きな種が特徴的な、肉厚のトロピカルフルーツです。このような果物の輸入は今後しばらく滞るに違いないので、早めに食べてしまいましょう。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "pomegranate"
msgid_plural "pomegranates"
msgstr[0] "ザクロ"

#. ~ Description of "pomegranate"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "Under this pomegranate's spongy skin lie hundreds of fleshy seeds."
msgstr "スポンジ状の皮を剥くと、果肉を付けた何百もの種が入っています。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "papaya"
msgid_plural "papayas"
msgstr[0] "パパイヤ"

#. ~ Description of "papaya"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A very sweet and soft tropical fruit."
msgstr "柔らかくて、非常に甘い南国の果物です。"

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Plant name of seed "kiwi seeds"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
#: data/mods/TropiCataclysm/items/comestibles/seed.json
msgid "kiwi"
msgid_plural "kiwis"
msgstr[0] "キウイフルーツ"

#. ~ Description of "kiwi"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"A large, brown, and fuzzy-skinned berry.  Its delicious insides are green."
msgstr "薄い毛で覆われた茶色の大きな果実です。中には緑色の美味しい果肉が入っています。"

#. ~ a handful of apricots is about 4.6 apricots
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "apricots"
msgid_plural "apricots"
msgstr[0] "アンズ"

#. ~ a handful of apricots is about 4.6 apricots
#. ~ Description of "apricots"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "A handful of smooth-skinned fruits related to the peach."
msgstr "滑らかな肌触りのモモに似た皮をもつ果物です。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "cholla bud"
msgid_plural "cholla buds"
msgstr[0] "サボテンの芽"

#. ~ Description of "cholla bud"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid ""
"The edible bud of a cholla cactus, with its spines removed; the candy of the"
" Mojave indigenous peoples.  Tastes similar to asparagus."
msgstr "モハーヴェ族がお菓子として食べる、棘を取り除いたチョヤサボテンの芽です。アスパラガスに似た味がします。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "cactus pad"
msgid_plural "cactus pads"
msgstr[0] "茎節(サボテン)"

#. ~ Description of "cactus pad"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_fruit.json
msgid "An edible pad from a cactus."
msgstr "サボテンから採取した食べられる茎節です。"

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Plant name of seed "barley seeds"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
#: data/json/items/comestibles/seed.json
msgid "barley"
msgid_plural "barley"
msgstr[0] "大麦"

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Plant name of seed "bee balm seeds"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
#: data/json/items/comestibles/seed.json
msgid "bee balm"
msgid_plural "bee balm"
msgstr[0] "ビーバーム"

#. ~ Description of "bee balm"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A snow-white flower also known as wild bergamot.  Smells faintly of mint."
msgstr "ワイルドベルガモットという通称で知られており、雪のように白い花をつけます。ほんのりとミントのような香りがします。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "handful of ground nuts"
msgid_plural "handful of ground nuts"
msgstr[0] "ホドイモ"

#. ~ Description of "handful of ground nuts"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"An almost forgotten staple of the native tribes, called the indian potato by"
" some.  Very nutritious, but mildly toxic unless cooked."
msgstr "インディアンポテトとも呼ばれる、今やほとんど食べられていない先住民の主食です。栄養価は高いですが、毒性があるため生食は危険です。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "wild sarsaparilla root"
msgid_plural "wild sarsaparilla roots"
msgstr[0] "根(ワイルドサルサパリラ)"

#. ~ Description of "wild sarsaparilla root"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"This aromatic rhizome can be eaten as is in an emergency, but it is much "
"better used for making beverages.  Its taste is pleasant but it is also "
"tough and stringy."
msgstr ""
"香りのよい根茎です。非常時にはそのまま食べてもいいですが、煎じて飲む方がずっと美味しいです。味は悪くありませんが、筋が多く硬いのが難点です。"

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Plant name of seed "Jerusalem artichoke seeds"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
#: data/json/items/comestibles/seed.json
msgid "Jerusalem artichoke"
msgid_plural "Jerusalem artichokes"
msgstr[0] "キクイモ"

#. ~ Description of "Jerusalem artichoke"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A slightly sweet tuber.  Contains much inulin which may cause some minor "
"issues with your digestive tract, so it should be cooked."
msgstr "ほんのりと甘い塊茎です。消化器に負担をかけるイヌリンを多く含んでいるため、加熱調理してから食べる必要があります。"

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Plant name of seed "wild garlic seeds"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
#: data/json/items/comestibles/seed.json
msgid "wild garlic"
msgid_plural "wild garlic"
msgstr[0] "ヒラタマネギ"

#. ~ Description of "wild garlic"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"Also called ramps, this delicate leafy vegetable is healthy and a tasty "
"ingredient for many dishes."
msgstr "ランプとも呼ばれる、細い葉野菜です。栄養価が高く美味しいため、様々な料理に使われます。"

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Plant name of seed "broccoli seeds"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
#: data/json/items/comestibles/seed.json
msgid "broccoli"
msgid_plural "broccoli"
msgstr[0] "ブロッコリー"

#. ~ Description of "broccoli"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A big stalk of broccoli.  It's a bit tough, but rich in Vitamin C and quite "
"delicious when properly cooked."
msgstr "太い茎をもつブロッコリーです。少し硬いですが、ビタミンCが豊富で、ちゃんと火を通せば美味しく食べられます。"

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Plant name of seed "buckwheat seeds"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
#: data/json/items/comestibles/seed.json
msgid "buckwheat"
msgid_plural "buckwheat"
msgstr[0] "蕎麦"

#. ~ Description of "buckwheat"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"Seeds from a wild buckwheat plant.  Not particularly good to eat in their "
"raw state, they are commonly cooked or ground into flour."
msgstr "野生の蕎麦の種です。そのままでは食べられたものではありません。調理するか挽いて粉にして使います。"

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Plant name of seed "cabbage seeds"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
#: data/json/items/comestibles/seed.json
msgid "cabbage"
msgid_plural "cabbages"
msgstr[0] "キャベツ"

#. ~ Description of "cabbage"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A head of crisp white cabbage."
msgstr "シャキシャキとした歯ごたえのホワイトキャベツです。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "grape leaves"
msgid_plural "grape leaves"
msgstr[0] "ブドウの葉"

#. ~ Description of "grape leaves"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"Edible leaves of the grape vine.  Typically used in salads or as a food "
"wrapping."
msgstr "食用になるブドウの葉です。サラダの材料や料理の包みに使われるのが一般的です。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "spinach"
msgid_plural "spinach"
msgstr[0] "ホウレンソウ"

#. ~ Description of "spinach"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A bunch of spinach leaves.  Their ability to provide one with superhuman "
"strength has been greatly exaggerated by popular media."
msgstr "一把のほうれん草です。超人的な強さをもたらすという話もありますが、それは有力メディアによる誇張表現です。"

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Plant name of seed "carrot seeds"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
#: data/json/items/comestibles/seed.json
msgid "carrot"
msgid_plural "carrots"
msgstr[0] "ニンジン"

#. ~ Description of "carrot"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A healthy root vegetable.  Rich in vitamin A!"
msgstr "健康的な根菜です。ビタミンAが豊富に含まれています！"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "cattail rhizome"
msgid_plural "cattail rhizomes"
msgstr[0] "ガマの根茎"

#. ~ Description of "cattail rhizome"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A stout, branching rhizome from a cattail plant.  Its crisp white flesh is "
"very starchy and fibrous, but you really ought to cook it before you attempt"
" to eat it."
msgstr "枝分かれしているガマの根茎です。白色の果肉は歯ごたえがあり、デンプン質と繊維質を豊富に含んでいますが、調理してから食べるべきです。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "cattail stalk"
msgid_plural "cattail stalks"
msgstr[0] "ガマの茎"

#. ~ Description of "cattail stalk"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A stiff green stalk from a cattail plant.  It is starchy and fibrous, but it"
" would be much better if you cooked it."
msgstr "ガマの茎です。堅くて緑色をしています。デンプン質と繊維を非常に多く含みます。食べるなら調理したほうがいいでしょう。"

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Plant name of seed "celery seeds"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
#: data/json/items/comestibles/seed.json
msgid "celery"
msgid_plural "celery"
msgstr[0] "セロリ"

#. ~ Description of "celery"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "Neither tasty nor very nutritious, but it goes well with salad."
msgstr "美味しくもなく栄養もそれほど豊富ではありませんが、サラダにはよく合います。"

#. ~ Thinking this is a single ear here.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "corn cob"
msgid_plural "corn cobs"
msgstr[0] "トウモロコシ"

#. ~ Thinking this is a single ear here.
#. ~ Description of "corn cob"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A corn cob full of delicious golden kernels.  You can eat them on the cob or"
" shell it for cooking."
msgstr "黄金色のコーンがたっぷり詰まったトウモロコシです。そのまま調理して食べてもいいですが、コーン粒を外して料理の材料に使うこともできます。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "corn kernels"
msgid_plural "corn kernels"
msgstr[0] "コーン粒"

#. ~ Description of "corn kernels"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "Delicious golden kernels of corn."
msgstr "黄金色に輝く美味しいトウモロコシです。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "empty corn cob"
msgid_plural "empty corn cob"
msgstr[0] "トウモロコシ軸"

#. ~ Description of "empty corn cob"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"An empty corn cob.  No longer contains any edible kernels, but it can be "
"used to make stock or as fuel."
msgstr "トウモロコシの軸です。もう食べられる実は付いていませんが、出汁の材料や燃料として利用できます。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "cotton boll"
msgid_plural "cotton bolls"
msgstr[0] "綿の実"

#. ~ Description of "cotton boll"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A tough protective capsule bulging with densely-packed fibers and seeds, "
"this cotton boll can be processed into usable material with the right tools."
msgstr "内部に繊維と種がぎっしりと詰まっている、硬い殻に覆われた綿の実です。適切な道具を使えば役立つ素材を採取できます。"

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Plant name of seed "chili pepper seeds"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
#: data/json/items/comestibles/seed.json
msgid "chili pepper"
msgid_plural "chili peppers"
msgstr[0] "トウガラシ"

#. ~ Description of "chili pepper"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A spicy chili pepper.  Not the best on its own, but adds great flavor when "
"used in cooking."
msgstr "スパイシーな唐辛子です。そのまま食べても美味しくありませんが、料理に入れると風味が増します。"

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Plant name of seed "cucumber seeds"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
#: data/json/items/comestibles/seed.json
msgid "cucumber"
msgid_plural "cucumbers"
msgstr[0] "キュウリ"

#. ~ Description of "cucumber"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A vegetable from the gourd family.  Not especially flavorful, but very "
"refreshing."
msgstr "ウリ科の野菜です。味はそれほどありませんが、瑞々しい歯ごたえです。"

#. ~ Dahlia roots contain an incredible amount of vitamin B6. This isn't a
#. vitamin tracked in Cataclysm, but be careful of vitamin overdose when
#. eating dahlia in real life.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "dahlia root"
msgid_plural "dahlia roots"
msgstr[0] "根(ダリア)"

#. ~ Dahlia roots contain an incredible amount of vitamin B6. This isn't a
#. vitamin tracked in Cataclysm, but be careful of vitamin overdose when
#. eating dahlia in real life.
#. ~ Description of "dahlia root"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"The large, tuberous root of a dahlia flower.  It smells spicy, but is too "
"starchy to eat without cooking."
msgstr "大きなダリアの塊根です。香ばしい匂いがしますが、デンプンが多すぎて生食には向きません。"

#. ~ Serving Size is 1 cup of sliced roots. Salsify grows in bountiful clumps,
#. it's a weed.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "salsify root"
msgid_plural "salsify roots"
msgstr[0] "根(サルシファイ)"

#. ~ Serving Size is 1 cup of sliced roots. Salsify grows in bountiful clumps,
#. it's a weed.
#. ~ Description of "salsify root"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A highly nutritious root, it is tough and bland until cooked, at which point"
" it tastes strangely similar to oysters."
msgstr "栄養価の高い根菜です。そのまま食べても硬く薄味ですが、加熱すると何故かオイスターのような風味が出ます。"

#. ~ Description of "chicory"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A modest blue flower.  The flower's roots are very bitter and not meant to "
"be eaten raw."
msgstr "可憐な青い花をつける野草です。根は苦みが強く、生食には向きません。"

#. ~ Also known as Queen Anne's Lace. It's that boring white flower that grows
#. wild everywhere. Water hemlock looks almost exactly like wild carrot. The
#. easiest way to tell them apart is by their scent. Please don't eat either
#. of them at home, hemlock will kill you deader than Socrates.
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Plant name of seed "wild root seeds"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
#: data/json/items/comestibles/seed.json
msgid "wild root"
msgid_plural "wild roots"
msgstr[0] "根菜"

#. ~ Also known as Queen Anne's Lace. It's that boring white flower that grows
#. wild everywhere. Water hemlock looks almost exactly like wild carrot. The
#. easiest way to tell them apart is by their scent. Please don't eat either
#. of them at home, hemlock will kill you deader than Socrates.
#. ~ Description of "wild root"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"These are often wild carrots, but beware of poisonous lookalikes.  In any "
"case, the root is tough and is not as tasty as a real raw carrot."
msgstr ""
"大抵はノラニンジンですが、似た外見で毒のある植物に気を付ける必要があります。いずれにせよ根が硬いため、生のニンジンほどは美味しく食べられません。"

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Plant name of seed "dogbane seeds"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
#: data/json/items/comestibles/seed.json
msgid "dogbane"
msgid_plural "dogbanes"
msgstr[0] "ドッグベイン"

#. ~ Description of "dogbane"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A stalk of dogbane.  It has very fibrous stems and is mildly poisonous."
msgstr "ドッグベインの茎です。繊維質が非常に多く、若干の毒性があります。"

#. ~ Who in their right mind would eat an entire garlic bulb raw?
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "garlic bulb"
msgid_plural "garlic bulbs"
msgstr[0] "ニンニク"

#. ~ Who in their right mind would eat an entire garlic bulb raw?
#. ~ Description of "garlic bulb"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A pungent garlic bulb.  Popular as a seasoning for its strong flavor.  Can "
"be disassembled into cloves."
msgstr "辛味のあるニンニクです。香りが強いため、調味料として人気があります。球根を更に小さな小鱗茎に分解できます。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "hops flower"
msgid_plural "hops flowers"
msgstr[0] "ホップの花"

#. ~ Description of "hops flower"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A cluster of small cone-like flowers, indispensable for brewing beer."
msgstr "小さな円錐形の毬花です。ビールの醸造には欠かせません。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "horseradish root"
msgid_plural "horseradish roots"
msgstr[0] "ホースラディッシュ"

#. ~ Description of "horseradish root"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A large white tapered root of a horseradish plant.  Way too spicy to eat in "
"this form, but can be used for making condiments."
msgstr "ワサビ科の植物から採れた、白く細長い根です。そのままでは辛すぎて食べられませんが、調味料の材料になります。"

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Plant name of seed "lettuce seeds"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
#: data/json/items/comestibles/seed.json
msgid "lettuce"
msgid_plural "lettuces"
msgstr[0] "レタス"

#. ~ Description of "lettuce"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A crisp head of iceberg lettuce."
msgstr "新鮮なアイスバーグレタスです。"

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Plant name of seed "mugwort seeds"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
#: data/json/items/comestibles/seed.json
msgid "mugwort"
msgid_plural "mugworts"
msgstr[0] "ヨモギ"

#. ~ Description of "mugwort"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A stalk of mugwort.  Smells wonderful."
msgstr "ヨモギの茎です。良い香りがします。"

#. ~ Raw onions probably aren't all that tasty to most people.
#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Plant name of seed "onion seeds"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
#: data/json/items/comestibles/seed.json
msgid "onion"
msgid_plural "onions"
msgstr[0] "タマネギ"

#. ~ Raw onions probably aren't all that tasty to most people.
#. ~ Description of "onion"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"An aromatic onion used in cooking.  Cutting these up can make your eyes "
"sting!"
msgstr "料理に使用する香り高いタマネギです。タマネギを切ると目に染みます！"

#. ~ wild vegetables as a reference
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "fungal fluid sac"
msgid_plural "fungal fluid sacs"
msgstr[0] "真菌流体嚢"

#. ~ wild vegetables as a reference
#. ~ Description of "fungal fluid sac"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A fluid bladder from a fungus-based lifeform.  Not very nutritious, but safe"
" to eat."
msgstr "真菌生命体から採取された、液体を溜める袋です。栄養価は高くありませんが、食べても問題はありません。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "raw popcorn"
msgid_plural "raw popcorn"
msgstr[0] "ポップコーン粒"

#. ~ Description of "raw popcorn"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A special variety of corn which could be used for making popcorn, after it's"
" dried.  Unlike normal corn, it's not sweet and is more dry."
msgstr "ポップコーンを作るための特別な品種のトウモロコシの実を乾燥させたものです。普通のトウモロコシより甘みは少なく、硬くなっています。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "raw potato"
msgid_plural "raw potatoes"
msgstr[0] "ジャガイモ"

#. ~ Description of "raw potato"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A potato, mildly toxic and not very tasty raw.  Delicious and filling when "
"properly cooked."
msgstr "ジャガイモは生で食べると弱い毒があり、あまり美味しくもありません。調理すると美味しくなり、食べ応えも増します。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "cooking banana"
msgid_plural "cooking bananas"
msgstr[0] "プランテン"

#. ~ Description of "cooking banana"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A much less sweet and more starchy relative of the banana; unlike dessert "
"bananas, they usually are eaten cooked rather than raw, and can be processed"
" into flour.  They are a staple food in tropical regions of the world.  Also"
" known as plantains."
msgstr ""
"バナナより甘味が少なくデンプン質が多い、バナナの仲間です。クッキングバナナという別名はありますが、バナナのように生食はせず加熱調理して食べるのが一般的で、粉に加工することもできます。特に熱帯地方で、主食として流通しています。"

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Plant name of seed "pumpkin seeds"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
#: data/json/items/comestibles/seed.json
msgid "pumpkin"
msgid_plural "pumpkins"
msgstr[0] "カボチャ"

#. ~ Description of "pumpkin"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A large gourd, about the size of your head.  Not very tasty raw, but great "
"for cooking."
msgstr "人間の頭ほどのサイズの野菜です。生ではあまり美味しくありませんが、調理すると非常に美味しく食べられます。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "horseradish greens"
msgid_plural "horseradish greens"
msgstr[0] "ホースラディッシュの葉"

#. ~ Description of "horseradish greens"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"Leaves of a horseradish plant with a sharp, bitter and peppery taste.  "
"They're edible, but not commonly eaten."
msgstr "キレのある苦みと胡椒のような風味が特徴的な、ワサビ科の植物の葉です。食べることも可能ですが、あまり一般的ではありません。"

#. ~ Description of "dandelion"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A handful of freshly-picked yellow dandelions.  In their current raw state "
"they are quite bitter."
msgstr "摘みたての黄色いタンポポの束です。生でそのまま食べても苦いだけです。"

#. ~ Description of "burdock"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "Burdock, a bitter thistle-like vegetable.  Can be eaten raw or cooked."
msgstr "アザミのような姿の、苦みの強い野菜です。生でも調理しても食べられます。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "bamboo shoot"
msgid_plural "bamboo shoot"
msgstr[0] "タケノコ"

#. ~ Description of "bamboo shoot"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"Raw woody bamboo shoots, they require some preparation before they can be "
"eaten safely."
msgstr "生のタケノコです。安全に食べるには、ある程度調理する必要があります。"

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Plant name of seed "rhubarb stems"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
#: data/json/items/comestibles/seed.json
msgid "rhubarb"
msgid_plural "rhubarbs"
msgstr[0] "ルバーブ"

#. ~ Description of "rhubarb"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "Sour stems of the rhubarb plant, often used in baking pies."
msgstr "茎に強い酸味のある食用の植物で、焼き菓子やパイ、ジャム等に使われます。"

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Plant name of seed "sugar beet seeds"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
#: data/json/items/comestibles/seed.json
msgid "sugar beet"
msgid_plural "sugar beets"
msgstr[0] "サトウダイコン"

#. ~ Description of "sugar beet"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"This fleshy root is ripe and flowing with sugars; it'll just take some "
"processing to extract them."
msgstr "熟した肉厚の根には糖分が含まれていますが、抽出するためには適切な加工が必要です。"

#. ~ Tea is sold by weight not by volume. 1 kg of tea has a volume of 3,4
#. liters. We use smaller packs of at least 100 mg. Such a tea has a volume of
#. 340 ml minus package makes it around 320 ml. 3 g per serving makes 33
#. charges.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "black tea leaf"
msgid_plural "black tea leaves"
msgstr[0] "紅茶葉"

#. ~ Tea is sold by weight not by volume. 1 kg of tea has a volume of 3,4
#. liters. We use smaller packs of at least 100 mg. Such a tea has a volume of
#. 340 ml minus package makes it around 320 ml. 3 g per serving makes 33
#. charges.
#. ~ Description of "black tea leaf"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"Dried leaves of a tropical plant.  You can boil them into tea, or you can "
"just eat them raw.  They're pretty gross and not too filling that way, "
"though."
msgstr "煮出すと紅茶になる、乾燥させた熱帯植物の葉です。そのまま食べても大丈夫ですが、美味しくもなく、空腹も満たせません。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "pile of wintergreen leaves"
msgid_plural "piles of wintergreen leaves"
msgstr[0] "ウィンターグリーンの葉"

#. ~ Description of "pile of wintergreen leaves"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"These leaves smell strongly medicinal.  When chewed, they first taste sweet "
"but the aftertaste is incredibly bitter.  These leaves contain good amounts "
"of methyl salicylate and merely chewing them may have a similar effect to "
"aspirin."
msgstr ""
"薬草の強い香りが漂う葉です。噛むと甘味を感じますが、後味には驚くほど強い苦味があります。サリチル酸メチルを多く含んでおり、噛むだけでアスピリンと同様の効果が期待できます。"

#. ~ "activation_message" action message of item "pile of wintergreen leaves"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "You chew the wintergreen leaves."
msgstr "ウィンターグリーンの葉を咀嚼しました。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "green tea leaf"
msgid_plural "green tea leaves"
msgstr[0] "緑茶葉"

#. ~ Description of "green tea leaf"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"Dried leaves of a tropical plant.  You can boil them into green tea, or you "
"can just eat them raw.  They're pretty gross and not too filling that way, "
"though."
msgstr "煮出すと緑茶になる、乾燥させた熱帯植物の葉です。そのまま食べても大丈夫ですが、美味しくもなく、空腹も満たせません。"

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Plant name of seed "tomato seeds"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
#: data/json/items/comestibles/seed.json
msgid "tomato"
msgid_plural "tomatoes"
msgstr[0] "トマト"

#. ~ Description of "tomato"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A juicy red tomato.  It gained popularity in Italy after being brought back "
"from the New World."
msgstr "瑞々しい真っ赤なトマトです。新大陸からイタリアに持ち込まれ、そこで人気を博しました。"

#. ~ average of broccoli, cabbage, carrot, cattail_stalk, celery,
#. chili_pepper, cucumber, lettuce, onion, pumpkin, raw_dandelion, rhubarb,
#. sugar_beet, tomato, zucchini
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "plant marrow"
msgid_plural "plant marrows"
msgstr[0] "植物髄"

#. ~ average of broccoli, cabbage, carrot, cattail_stalk, celery,
#. chili_pepper, cucumber, lettuce, onion, pumpkin, raw_dandelion, rhubarb,
#. sugar_beet, tomato, zucchini
#. ~ Description of "plant marrow"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A nutrient-rich chunk of plant matter, could be eaten raw or cooked."
msgstr "栄養価の高い植物質です。生のままでも、調理をしても食べられます。"

#. ~ Note: Legacy item ID, this is not actually a vegetable at all anymore.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "alien fungus chunk"
msgid_plural "alien fungus chunks"
msgstr[0] "真菌塊"

#. ~ Note: Legacy item ID, this is not actually a vegetable at all anymore.
#. ~ Description of "alien fungus chunk"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"This is a chunk of fungal matter from some sort of alien mushroom creature."
"  Eating unfamiliar mushrooms is a bad idea."
msgstr "地球外から来たキノコの化け物を構成する真菌の塊です。馴染みのないキノコを食べるのは危険な考えです。"

#. ~ In real life many root vegetables are mildly toxic until cooked
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "wild vegetables"
msgid_plural "wild vegetables"
msgstr[0] "山菜"

#. ~ In real life many root vegetables are mildly toxic until cooked
#. ~ Description of "wild vegetables"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"An assortment of edible-looking wild plants.  Most are quite bitter-tasting."
"  Some are inedible until cooked."
msgstr "食用に適しているように見える雑草の束です。ほとんどが強い苦味を持ち、調理しなければ食べられない物も混じっています。"

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Plant name of seed "zucchini seeds"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
#: data/json/items/comestibles/seed.json
msgid "zucchini"
msgid_plural "zucchinis"
msgstr[0] "ズッキーニ"

#. ~ Description of "zucchini"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "A tasty summer squash."
msgstr "美味しい夏野菜です。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "raw beans"
msgid_plural "raw beans"
msgstr[0] "生豆"

#. ~ Description of "raw beans"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"Raw, uncooked beans.  They are mildly toxic in this form, but you could cook"
" them to make them tasty."
msgstr "未調理の生豆です。弱い毒性がありますが、調理すれば美味しく食べられます。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
#: data/json/items/comestibles/seed.json
msgid "raw lentils"
msgid_plural "raw lentils"
msgstr[0] "生レンズ豆"

#. ~ Description of "raw lentils"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "Raw, uncooked lentils."
msgstr "調理していない生のレンズ豆です。"

#. ~ Fiddleheads that haven't been boiled can make you sick.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "fiddleheads"
msgid_plural "fiddleheads"
msgstr[0] "ゼンマイ"

#. ~ Fiddleheads that haven't been boiled can make you sick.
#. ~ Description of "fiddleheads"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A handful of immature fern fronds, still curled up like the head of a "
"fiddle.  Delicious when cooked, but consuming them raw can cause food "
"poisoning."
msgstr ""
"未成熟なシダ植物の穂先の束です。バイオリンの頭のようにくるっと丸まっています。調理すれば美味しく食べられますが、生食は食中毒を起こす危険性があります。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "handful of young leaves"
msgid_plural "handful of young leaves"
msgstr[0] "若葉"

#. ~ Description of "handful of young leaves"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"Some young leaves from miscellaneous plants.  They're tender enough to eat, "
"but not very tasty raw."
msgstr "一握りの様々な植物の若葉です。無理なく食べられる柔らかさですが、生で食べても美味しくありません。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
#: data/json/items/comestibles/seed.json
msgid "Japanese knotweed stems"
msgid_plural "Japanese knotweed stems"
msgstr[0] "茎(イタドリ)"

#. ~ Description of "Japanese knotweed stems"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"Some young Japanese knotweed stems.  They taste a bit like rhubarb and "
"contain good amounts of vitamin A.  Refreshing."
msgstr "若いイタドリの茎です。ルバーブに似た爽やかな味わいがあり、ビタミンAを多く含みます。"

#. ~ Item name
#. ~ Plant name of seed "bell pepper seeds"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
#: data/json/items/comestibles/seed.json
msgid "bell pepper"
msgid_plural "bell peppers"
msgstr[0] "ピーマン"

#. ~ Description of "bell pepper"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"A green bell pepper.  Eating it whole and raw would be kind of a hassle, "
"considering all the seeds."
msgstr "緑色のピーマンです。種も取らずそのまま生で食べるのは、ちょっと困難です。"

#. ~ 240 ml is equivalent to 1 cup of flour.  10 charges is roughly equivalent
#. to a cup of flour for American recipes.
#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid "wheat-free flour"
msgid_plural "wheat-free flour"
msgstr[0] "グルテンフリー粉"

#. ~ 240 ml is equivalent to 1 cup of flour.  10 charges is roughly equivalent
#. to a cup of flour for American recipes.
#. ~ Description of "wheat-free flour"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/raw_veggy.json
msgid ""
"This wheat-free white flour is useful for baking items for those with grain "
"intolerances."
msgstr "グルテン不耐症でも食べられるパン作りに便利な、グルテンが入っていない精白粉です。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/sandwich.json
msgid "grilled cheese sandwich"
msgid_plural "grilled cheese sandwiches"
msgstr[0] "サンドイッチ(焼きﾁｰｽﾞ)"

#. ~ Description of "grilled cheese sandwich"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/sandwich.json
msgid ""
"A delicious grilled cheese sandwich, because everything is better with "
"melted cheese."
msgstr "美味しい焼きチーズのサンドイッチです。どんな料理でも美味しくなる、それがとろけるチーズというものです。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/sandwich.json
msgid "egg salad sandwich"
msgid_plural "egg salad sandwiches"
msgstr[0] "サンドイッチ(卵ｻﾗﾀﾞ)"

#. ~ Description of "egg salad sandwich"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/sandwich.json
msgid "A delicious egg salad sandwich."
msgstr "卵サラダを挟んだ美味しいサンドイッチです。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/sandwich.json
msgid "wheat free egg salad sandwich"
msgid_plural "wheat free egg salad sandwiches"
msgstr[0] "穀物不使用サンドイッチ(卵ｻﾗﾀﾞ)"

#. ~ Description of "wheat free egg salad sandwich"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/sandwich.json
msgid "A delicious egg salad sandwich on wheat-free bread."
msgstr "穀物が入っていないパンで作った、卵サラダを挟んだ美味しいサンドイッチです。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/sandwich.json
msgid "deluxe sandwich"
msgid_plural "deluxe sandwiches"
msgstr[0] "サンドイッチ(DX)"

#. ~ Description of "deluxe sandwich"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/sandwich.json
msgid ""
"A sandwich of meat, vegetables, and cheese with condiments.  Tasty and "
"nutritious!"
msgstr "肉、野菜、チーズ、そして各種の調味料を挟んだ豪華版サンドイッチです。味も栄養も抜群です！"

#. ~ Conditional name for "deluxe sandwich" when COMPONENT_ID_SUBSTRING
#. matches mutant
#: data/json/items/comestibles/sandwich.json
msgid "\"deluxe\" sandwich"
msgid_plural "\"deluxe\" sandwiches"
msgstr[0] "サンドイッチ(変異DX)"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/sandwich.json
msgid "reuben sandwich"
msgid_plural "reuben sandwiches"
msgstr[0] "ルーベンサンド"

#. ~ Description of "reuben sandwich"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/sandwich.json
msgid ""
"A pre-Cataclysm classic, probably made with significant substitutions.  Key "
"components are the special sauce and sauerkraut, with bread, meat, and "
"cheese fried in a pan."
msgstr ""
"大変動以前からの定番料理ですが、おそらく材料のほとんどは代用品です。一般的には、パンに特製ソースとザワークラウト、肉、チーズを挟み、フライパンで焼いて作ります。"

#. ~ Conditional name for "reuben sandwich" when COMPONENT_ID_SUBSTRING
#. matches mutant
#: data/json/items/comestibles/sandwich.json
msgid "\"fauxben\" sandwich"
msgid_plural "\"fauxben\" sandwiches"
msgstr[0] "変異ルーベンサンド"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/sandwich.json
msgid "cucumber sandwich"
msgid_plural "cucumber sandwiches"
msgstr[0] "サンドイッチ(ｷｭｳﾘ)"

#. ~ Description of "cucumber sandwich"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/sandwich.json
msgid "A refreshing cucumber sandwich.  Not very filling, but quite tasty."
msgstr "爽やかなキュウリのサンドイッチです。食べ応えはありませんが、スッキリとした美味しさです。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/sandwich.json
msgid "cheese sandwich"
msgid_plural "cheese sandwiches"
msgstr[0] "サンドイッチ(ﾁｰｽﾞ)"

#. ~ Description of "cheese sandwich"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/sandwich.json
msgid "A simple cheese sandwich."
msgstr "チーズを挟んだシンプルなサンドイッチです。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/sandwich.json
msgid "jam sandwich"
msgid_plural "jam sandwiches"
msgstr[0] "サンドイッチ(ｼﾞｬﾑ)"

#. ~ Description of "jam sandwich"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/sandwich.json
msgid "A delicious jam sandwich."
msgstr "ジャムを挟んだ美味しいサンドイッチです。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/sandwich.json
msgid "jam and cheese sandwich"
msgid_plural "jam and cheese sandwiches"
msgstr[0] "サンドイッチ(ｼﾞｬﾑﾁｰｽﾞ)"

#. ~ Description of "jam and cheese sandwich"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/sandwich.json
msgid "A delicious jam and cheese sandwich."
msgstr "ジャムとチーズを挟んだ美味しいサンドイッチです。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/sandwich.json
msgid "jam and butter sandwich"
msgid_plural "jam and butter sandwiches"
msgstr[0] "サンドイッチ(ｼﾞｬﾑﾊﾞﾀｰ)"

#. ~ Description of "jam and butter sandwich"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/sandwich.json
msgid "A delicious jam and butter sandwich."
msgstr "ジャムとバターを挟んだ美味しいサンドイッチです。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/sandwich.json
msgid "fairy bread"
msgid_plural "fairy bread"
msgstr[0] "フェアリーブレッド"

#. ~ Description of "fairy bread"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/sandwich.json
msgid ""
"An 'open-faced sandwich' consisting of sliced white bread, a healthy crust-"
"to-crust slathering of butter, and sprinkles.  Supposedly a staple of "
"birthday parties in Australia."
msgstr ""
"パンをスライスし、バターを塗って大量のスプリンクルをまぶした「オープンサンドイッチ」です。オーストラリアの誕生日パーティーでは定番のようです。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/sandwich.json
msgid "honey sandwich"
msgid_plural "honey sandwiches"
msgstr[0] "サンドイッチ(蜂蜜)"

#. ~ Description of "honey sandwich"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/sandwich.json
msgid "A delicious honey sandwich."
msgstr "蜂蜜を塗った美味しいサンドイッチです。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/sandwich.json
msgid "boring sandwich"
msgid_plural "boring sandwiches"
msgstr[0] "サンドイッチ(ｿｰｽ)"

#. ~ Description of "boring sandwich"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/sandwich.json
msgid ""
"A simple sauce sandwich.  Not very filling, but it beats eating just the "
"bread."
msgstr "ソースを塗っただけのサンドイッチです。物足りませんが、ただパンを貪るよりはマシです。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/sandwich.json
msgid "vegetable sandwich"
msgid_plural "vegetable sandwiches"
msgstr[0] "サンドイッチ(野菜)"

#. ~ Description of "vegetable sandwich"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/sandwich.json
msgid "Bread and vegetables, that's it."
msgstr "パンと野菜、それだけです。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/sandwich.json
msgid "vegetable sandwich with cheese"
msgid_plural "vegetable sandwiches with cheese"
msgstr[0] "サンドイッチ(野菜とチーズ)"

#. ~ Description of "vegetable sandwich with cheese"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/sandwich.json
msgid ""
"A vegetarian combination of cheese and vegetable on bread, simple yet "
"satisfying."
msgstr "チーズと野菜をパンで挟んだ、ベジタリアンでも食べられるシンプルながら満足度の高いサンドイッチです。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/sandwich.json
msgid "gluten free vegetable sandwich with cheese"
msgid_plural "gluten free vegetable sandwiches with cheese"
msgstr[0] "穀物不使用サンドイッチ(野菜とチーズ)"

#. ~ Description of "gluten free vegetable sandwich with cheese"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/sandwich.json
msgid ""
"A gluten free vegetarian combination of cheese and vegetable on bread, "
"simple yet satisfying."
msgstr "チーズと野菜をグルテンフリーのパンで挟んだ、ベジタリアンでも食べられるシンプルながら満足度の高いサンドイッチです。"

#. ~ Item name
#: data/json/items/comestibles/sandwich.json
msgid "meat sandwich"
msgid_plural "meat sandwiches"
msgstr[0] "サンドイッチ(肉)"

#. ~ Description of "meat sandwich"
#: data/json/items/comestibles/sandwich.json
msgid "Bread and meat, that's it."
msgstr "パンと肉、それだけです。"

#. ~ Conditional name for "meat sandwich" when FLAG matches CANNIBALISM
#: data/json/items/comestibles/sandwich.json
