#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_COMPUTER.json
#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_TRAIN_DATA.json
msgid "The computer awaits input…"
msgstr "コンピュータは入力待ちの状態です..."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_COMPUTER.json
msgid "Emergency Message."
msgstr "緊急メッセージ閲覧"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#. ~ Mission name
#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_COMPUTER.json
#: data/json/obsoletion/npcs/necropolis/NPC_Old_Guard_Commo.json
msgid "Disable External Power"
msgstr "外部電力を無効化する"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_COMPUTER.json
msgid "Contact Us"
msgstr "お問い合わせ"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_COMPUTER.json
msgid "Log off."
msgstr "ログオフ"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_COMPUTER.json
msgid ""
"GREETINGS CITIZEN.  A BIOLOGICAL ATTACK HAS TAKEN PLACE AND A STATE OF EMERGENCY HAS BEEN DECLARED.  EMERGENCY PERSONNEL WILL BE AIDING YOU SHORTLY.  TO ENSURE YOUR SAFETY PLEASE FOLLOW THE STEPS BELOW.\n"
" 1. DO NOT PANIC.\n"
" 2. REMAIN INSIDE THE BUILDING.\n"
" 3. SEEK SHELTER IN THE BASEMENT.\n"
" 4. USE PROVIDED GAS MASKS.\n"
" 5. AWAIT FURTHER INSTRUCTIONS."
msgstr ""
"国民の皆様へ\n"
"生物攻撃が発生し、国家非常事態宣言が発令されています。まもなく救助隊が到着します。安全確保のため、以下の手順に従って行動して下さい。\n"
"\n"
"1．慌てない。\n"
"2．建物の外に出ない。\n"
"3．地下に避難する。\n"
"4．備品のガスマスクを着用する。\n"
"5．指示があるまで待機する。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_COMPUTER.json
msgid "Press any key."
msgstr "キーを押す。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_COMPUTER.json
msgid ""
"--ACCESS GRANTED--\n"
"Mission Complete!"
msgstr ""
"--アクセス許可--\n"
"ミッション完了！"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_COMPUTER.json
msgid ""
"REFUGEE CENTER FOUND!  IF YOU HAVE ANY FEEDBACK CONCERNING YOUR VISIT PLEASE CONTACT\n"
" THE DEPARTMENT OF EMERGENCY MANAGEMENT PUBLIC AFFAIRS OFFICE.\n"
" THE LOCAL OFFICE CAN BE REACHED BETWEEN THE HOURS OF 9AM AND\n"
" 4PM AT 555-0164.\n"
"\n"
"IF YOU WOULD LIKE TO SPEAK WITH SOMEONE IN PERSON OR WOULD LIKE\n"
"TO WRITE US A LETTER PLEASE SEND IT TO…"
msgstr ""
"避難センターを発見しました！ご意見がございましたら\n"
"緊急管理部広報課へご連絡ください。\n"
"現地事務所対応時間　9:00～16:00\n"
"電話番号　555-0164\n"
"直接のご訪問やお手紙はこちらまで..."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_COMPUTER.json
msgid "Make a note of the location."
msgstr "所在地をメモする。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_NURSING_HOME.json
msgid ""
"Shady Hills Nursing Home.\n"
" You are logged in as: Joe Shert, Receptionist.\n"
"\n"
"WARNING!  ERROR A101; FAILURE DETECTED IN POWER SUPPLY.\n"
" RESERVE POWER ACTIVATED.  CONTACT INFORMATION TECHNOLOGY DEPARTMENT IMMEDIATELY!"
msgstr ""
"シェイディヒルズ老人ホーム\n"
" ログイン中: ジョー・シェルト、受付係\n"
"\n"
"警告！エラー A101; 電源に障害が検出されました。\n"
" 予備電源が稼働しました。情報技術担当者にご連絡ください！"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_NURSING_HOME.json
msgid "Access Assigned Tasks"
msgstr "タスクにアクセス"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_NURSING_HOME.json
msgid "RE: Ghosts!?"
msgstr "RE: 幽霊！？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_NURSING_HOME.json
msgid "RE: Performance Evaluation"
msgstr "RE: 勤務評価の件"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_NURSING_HOME.json
msgid "RE: Mrs.  Palmero"
msgstr "RE: パルメロ様"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_NURSING_HOME.json
msgid "RE: Housekeeping"
msgstr "RE: 清掃部門の件"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_NURSING_HOME.json
msgid ""
"FROM: Connie Malackey, Receptionist\n"
" TO: Joe Shert, Receptionist\n"
" RE: Ghosts!?\n"
"\n"
" Joe!  After we heard those weird noises the other night, I talked to some of the nurses.\n"
" We aren't the only ones!  Everyone has heard weird noises coming from the walls.\n"
" Do you think this place is haunted!?"
msgstr ""
"FROM: コニー・マラッキー、受付係\n"
" TO: ジョー・シェルト、受付係\n"
" RE: 幽霊！？\n"
"\n"
" ジョー！この間の夜、変な音がしたでしょう。あの後で看護師さんたちに話したんです。\n"
" 聞いたのは私たちだけじゃないみたい！みんな、壁から変な音がするのを聞いたんですって。\n"
" この施設には幽霊が出るのかしら！？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_NURSING_HOME.json
msgid ""
"FROM: Bryan Rooters, Reception Manager\n"
" TO: Joe Shert, Receptionist\n"
" RE: Performance Eval\n"
"\n"
" Hi Joe.\n"
" Your 90-day performance evaluation is due.  Please plan to meet with me in my office on Tuesday.\n"
" Thanks."
msgstr ""
"FROM: ブライアン・ローターズ、受付部門マネージャー\n"
" TO: ジョー・シェルト、受付係\n"
" RE: 勤務評価の件\n"
"\n"
" ジョーへ\n"
" 90日間の業績評価日を迎えました。次の火曜日に私のオフィスで面談を行うので、予定を空けておいてください。\n"
" よろしくお願いします。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_NURSING_HOME.json
msgid ""
"FROM: Bryan Rooters, Reception Manager\n"
" TO: Receptionists\n"
" RE: Housekeping\n"
"\n"
" Hi team,\n"
" Please be aware that the decision has been made to let go some of the housekeeping staff.\n"
" This decision was made by management to ensure that our operation can run as smoothly and efficiently as possible by passing on these cost savings to the residents.\n"
" To keep up with our high standards of elder care, I will be assigning some additional small tasks to you in the near future.\n"
" As you know, here at Shady Hills we value each and every employee and see this as an excellent opportunity to grow, learn, and provide for the Shady Hills family.\n"
" Please let me know if you have any questions.\n"
" Thanks."
msgstr ""
"FROM: ブライアン・ローターズ、受付部門マネージャー\n"
" TO: 受付部門\n"
" RE: 清掃部門の件\n"
"\n"
" 受付部門の皆へ\n"
" この度、清掃スタッフの一部を解雇することが決定したため、お知らせします。\n"
" このようなコスト削減を入所者の皆様へ還元し、可能な限り円滑かつ効率的な運営を目指すために、経営部門は今回の決定に至りました。\n"
" 高水準の高齢者ケアを維持するために、近い将来、受付部門のスタッフにもいくつか簡単な仕事を追加で割り当てる予定です。\n"
" 知っての通り、シェイディヒルズは従業員一人一人を尊重しており、皆に成長や学び、そしてシェイディヒルズへの貢献という得難い機会を提供しています。\n"
" 不明な点があれば連絡してください。\n"
" よろしくお願いします。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/computers/TALK_NURSING_HOME.json
msgid ""
"FROM: Connie Malackey, Receptionist\n"
" TO: Joe Shert, Receptionist\n"
" RE: Mrs.  Palmero\n"
"\n"
" Hi Joe.\n"
" So - you know how Mrs.  Palmero has been acting weird and constantly talking about baking cookies?\n"
" I was talking to one of the nurses and they said that Mrs.  Palmero was prescribed this new medicine?\n"
" It's this weird powder stuff.  Apparently the nurses aren't even qualified to give it to her - she needs a special doctor to come in every day!\n"
" Crazy, right?  I wish all I had to worry about was baking cookies…"
msgstr ""
"FROM: コニー・マラッキー、受付係\n"
" TO: ジョー・シェルト、受付係\n"
" RE: パルメロ様\n"
"\n"
"ねえ、ジョー。\n"
" その、パルメロ様の様子がちょっとおかしくて、クッキーを焼く話ばかりするのだけれど、何か知らない？\n"
" 看護師から聞いたんだけど、パルメロ様は新薬を処方されたんですって？\n"
" 新薬っていうのは、妙な粉末のこと。看護師は投与資格がないんですって。毎日ここへ来てる専門の医師しか投与できないらしいの！\n"
" ちょっと、変じゃない？クッキーを焼く話だけだったら、ここまで悩みもしないんだけど..."

