#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/valhalla_cult/valhallist_leader_backstory.json
msgid "I suppose I can trust you that much.  What do you want to know?"
msgstr "そろそろお前を信用してもいい頃合いか。何が知りたいのだ？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/valhalla_cult/valhallist_leader_backstory.json
msgid "How did you come to power here?"
msgstr "どうやってこの集団で権力を手にしたんだ？"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/valhalla_cult/valhallist_leader_backstory.json
msgid "When did you build this place?"
msgstr "いつこの集落を作ったんだ？"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/valhalla_cult/valhallist_leader_backstory.json
msgid ""
"I was a big history buff back then, but I worked in dead-end accounting for "
"a university.  I had three friends who I hung with after-hours; we were out "
"on the town when <the_cataclysm> came."
msgstr ""
"かつて、我は歴史学を愛してはいたが、大学の会計士として糊口を凌いでいた。<the_cataclysm>が来るまでは、仕事が終わると、特に仲のいい3人の友といつも街へ繰り出して遊んでいた。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/valhalla_cult/valhallist_leader_backstory.json
msgid ""
"One of my buddies wanted to get in the re-enacting business, so they started"
" setting up this place as a to-scale model of what a Norse fort might have "
"looked like.  I was planning on getting in to it with them, but "
"<the_cataclysm> put a stop to it.  We came here from town, found the place "
"wasn't occupied by those horrors, and set up camp here.  The Norse-obsessed "
"guy decided to make a full religion out of it, and managed to bring back a "
"large group fleeing one of those FEMA camps."
msgstr ""
"友人の一人が、歴史再現施設を作りたいと言い出し、この場所に実物大で再現された北欧の砦を建設することになった。我も作業に加わろうと思っていたが、その前に<the_cataclysm>が訪れ、建設は中止になった。我らは街から避難し、恐ろしい化け物共に侵されていないこの場所を拠点とすることにした。北欧神話に憑り付かれていた我は、この場所を聖地にすると決め、FEMAキャンプから逃げ出してきた避難者たちを仲間に迎え入れた。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/valhalla_cult/valhallist_leader_backstory.json
msgid ""
"One of my buddies was the head before me.  They were really interested in "
"Norse mythology, almost obsessed with it.  After <the_cataclysm>, they "
"started preaching to a group who ran from town, and set up here.  I followed"
" along, not wanting to abandon them in the wilderness."
msgstr ""
"友の一人が、我の先代の大長だった。我も友人も北欧神話にのめり込んでおり、ほとんど憑り付かれているような心境だった。<the_cataclysm>の後、街から逃げてきた者に神話の精神を伝道し、ここに住まわせた。我も避難者たちを荒野へ捨て置く訳にはいかぬと思い、この運動に協力したのだ。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/valhalla_cult/valhallist_leader_backstory.json
msgid ""
"We were out on a routine scavenging run one day, like we'd done many times "
"before.  Some horde followed us out of town, and we had to fight them off.  "
"Something was off about this one zombie though, huge and burly towards the "
"back.  We managed to handle the rest of them easy, but this one guy was a "
"bit much for the three of us…"
msgstr ""
"ある日、友らといつものように物資漁りに出かけた。途中で大群に街の外まで追い立てられ、撃退するほかない状況になってしまった。その中に混じっていた一体のゾンビが、妙な奴だったのだ。とにかく図体がデカい。他のゾンビ共は簡単に倒せたが、そやつだけは、3人がかりではどうにもならなかった..."

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/valhalla_cult/valhallist_leader_backstory.json
msgid "I'm guessing that didn't go well."
msgstr "退治できなかったのか。"

#. ~ NPC dialogue line
#: data/json/npcs/valhalla_cult/valhallist_leader_backstory.json
msgid ""
"*begins to weep, hanging their head down.*  \"I'm sorry, I couldn't save "
"them.  They all died to that horrid monster.  I buried all three of them, "
"and was chosen to rule by a will one of them left.  I realized then that my "
"friend was right; only the strong survive, and only the strong live long "
"enough to enjoy that."
msgstr ""
"*俯き、すすり泣き始める*「すまぬ、友よ。我は友を救えなかった。皆あの恐ろしい怪物に殺された。我は3人を埋葬し、そのうち1人が残していた遺言に従い、新たな大長となった。我が友の言葉を真に理解したのはその時だ。強き者だけが生き残る。強き者だけが長く生き、その生を享受できる。"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/valhalla_cult/valhallist_leader_backstory.json
msgid "I'm sorry for your loss.  <done_conversation_section>"
msgstr "辛い話だ。<done_conversation_section>"

#. ~ Response to NPC dialogue
#: data/json/npcs/valhalla_cult/valhallist_leader_backstory.json
msgid "I'm sorry for your loss, I should get going."
msgstr "辛い話だ。私はそろそろ失礼するよ。"

